{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c3d1","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c5d0-c246-7b92-beac-dc3b11390997"},"sequence":67,"recorded_at":1780531400000129,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"aa3bb7a1-c12a-4660-a0d5-ffba7d41ef0c","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"aa3bb7a1-c12a-4660-a0d5-ffba7d41ef0c","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"aa3bb7a1-c12a-4660-a0d5-ffba7d41ef0c"},"call_id":"call_01a0c5d0f49974169594f10eb408546b","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-35urbp/TASK-260830-35urbp_rework-rev7.md`.\n1|THIS BRIEF SUPERSEDES TASK-260830-35urbp_rework-rev6.md and every earlier precondition. Do exactly what is written here.\n2|Rework run for TASK-260830-35urbp. Revision 6 was reviewed by RUN-260921-a7163e (claude-opus-5 max) and routed CHANGES REQUESTED with **no P1**: one P2 and two P3. Read TASK-260830-35urbp_review-verdict-rev6.md first.\n3|**The census worked.** The reviewer confirms the gate × entry census you built exists, its counts reproduce mechanically (24 × 11 = 264 cells; 50 Measured / 4 Bound / 210 Unreachable), and its per-entry kill attribution holds for all 50 Measured cells. Every rev5 finding — the four broker-path members, the ownership member, the false \"before any side effect\", observations 1-6 — is closed with driven evidence and stays closed. **Production behaves correctly at every point this review drove; every surviving plant is killed by a probe that passes on the untouched candidate.** No production change in this revision. Keep everything.\n4|Trunk has NOT moved (base is still 799c338). Build revision 7 on the rev6 candidate. Do not refresh, do not rebase. This should be the last round: the remaining work is one harness row, three fixtures, two table-widenings and three doc sentences.\n5|\n6|1. **P2-A — the commit-side `O_DIRECTORY` arm has no narrowing row, and the census shows the asymmetry it did not flag.** The gate is implemented twice, commit (`runtime_unix.go:58-59`) and verify, with the same flags. In rev3 you gave the VERIFY side exactly the right treatment: a 0700 regular file (so a weakened open admits it outright instead of rerouting to the mode gate) and a FIFO under a deadline (so the no-hang property is pinned). The commit side never got it. Dropping `unix.O_DIRECTORY` from the commit `Openat` — the exact twin of your own `N-containment-odirectory-verify` — is KILLED, but **by reroute only**: `TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesNonDirectoryLeaf` uses a 0600 fixture, so the MODE gate catches what the containment gate stopped catching, and the failure message says `runtime mode` where it should say `runtime containment`. What the committed suite cannot see under that plant: a 0700 non-directory leaf is ADMITTED by `EnsureRuntimeDir` and through the foreground entry — which then probes the server and spawns into `<root>/tmux/ax.sock` where `tmux` is a regular file — and a FIFO leaf **BLOCKS the creating path for the full 5s deadline** on the writer-less `O_RDONLY` open. Ship: the verify side's fixtures on the commit side (a 0700 regular-file leaf on `EnsureRuntimeDir` and through foreground `Acquire`, asserting no probe and no spawn; a FIFO leaf on `EnsureRuntimeDir` under the existing `verifyWithDeadline`); the row `N-containment-odirectory-commit`, named under row 5 and in the `commit × ENS` and `commit × AFG` census cells; row 5's FIFO clause reworded to name both deadline tests; and the `N-containment-odirectory-verify` note corrected — it currently ASSERTS \"the commit side still refuses\" instead of pointing at a row that proves it.\n7|   **And run this check on the census itself before you hand off.** The instrument was the deliverable and it made the asymmetry visible — the `verify × VER` cell lists `N-containment-odirectory-verify` while the `commit × ENS` cell lists ten rows and none touches that arm — but nothing flagged it. The harness has three verify-side containment rows against two commit-side. So: for every gate implemented on two or more sides, compare the row sets side by side, and report the comparison as a short table in the results — gate, sides, rows per side, and either \"symmetric\" or the named missing row. A gate whose sides have different row counts is the finding this round was about, and the census should surface it without a reviewer.\n8|2. **P3-A — the no-fallback rule's platform axis is pinned at the miss arm for macOS and Linux only.** A fallback `Spawn` on the background MISS path guarded on WSL2 SURVIVED both passes: the miss tables drive macOS (8 shapes) and Linux (1 shape), and the only WSL2 background test refuses on the absent leaf BEFORE the miss arm, so no committed test reaches a WSL2 miss. The siblings are pinned — the same guard on Linux, WSL2 callers dispatched to the foreground path, and the absence remap withheld on WSL2 are all KILLED twice — so this is one member, not a class. It is also the same shape as rev4's P3-A one arm over. Make the Linux miss test a platform table `{linux, wsl2}` (or add a WSL2 subtest to the miss table), add it to `BG_MISS_LINUX` so `N-creation-literal` and both `D-` rows kill through all three tmux platforms, and name it under rows 29/31.\n9|3. **P3-B — the attestation membership arm is pinned for one decoy of a sixteen-value vocabulary.** Every committed decoy is `headless_creation`, so a narrowing keyed on any of the other fourteen non-realm capabilities walks through the helper, the broker contact and both `Acquire` paths — the reviewer's `local_attach` row SURVIVED twice. The independent source is already in the tree: `catalog.Current().Capabilities` IS the sixteen-value §4.D table. Derive the decoy set from the catalog rather than from a fixture constant, assert every non-realm capability alone and the whole set together, and state the completeness claim only where the derivation proves it.\n10|\n11|PROCESS. Keep the candidate UNCOMMITTED; exactly one leaf's worth of delta. Never commit on the Story branch, never edit `.task-board` directly, never self-accept, and do NOT touch `internal/traceability` — the final leaf g0pcnt carries the registry. Run your own package tests, `GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go vet ./...` (keep it green), and both harnesses BEFORE handoff, then the full configured suite once, reading the commands from `spawn.worktree_isolation.validation.commands` in the candidate config. A second Story is producing concurrently on this host, so command 5 will be slow; do NOT shorten it, and report measured elapsed time and host load if a gate times out. Update the results with a finding-by-finding table, the refreshed census with its measured ratio, and the new two-sided-gate symmetry table; update the conformance matrix and the evidence archive (a real gzip archive, MANIFEST with no self-entry, one raw log per plant with its subprocess exit, PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1, zero `__pycache__`), re-complete the checklist, then `task-board handoff TASK-260830-35urbp --role developer` so revision 7 is constructed, and exit promptly. Hand off no later than 2 hours in. Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board. Model: muse-spark max. The same claude-opus-5 max reviewer contract applies to revision 7.\n12|REJECTION PATTERNS THE INDEPENDENT REVIEWER HAS ALREADY CAUGHT ON THIS EPIC (2026-09-17: TASK-260830-1geqhj rev1, TASK-260830-24z2b3 rev2, TASK-260830-219okr rev3 were all routed CHANGES REQUESTED, and between them these six shapes account for every finding). Read this as a checklist you run against your own work BEFORE handoff; each item names what a reviewer will do to your candidate.\n13|(a) Circular expectations. An assertion that compares a production value against a production constant (`got.Code == pkg.SomeUnsupportedCode`) pins nothing: swapping the constant to another registered value with the same exit keeps the suite green. Assert the LITERAL token from the pinned specification text, at the production entry, and make sure the literal actually occurs in a committed test — not only in a comment. Derive every expectation from the spec, never from the implementation.\n14|(b) A rule pinned at the helper instead of the entry. A test that calls the inner helper directly proves the helper; it says nothing about whether the composed production entry still reaches it. Drive every rule through the entry point the conformance matrix names as its call site, and if a rule is implemented TWICE (a Build path and a Decode path, an exported entry and its internal sibling), each side needs its own narrowing mutant — a rule pinned only on one side leaves the other side unmeasured, and reviewers plant exactly there.\n15|(c) Forking a landed gate. Never re-implement what internal/environ, internal/canonicaljson, internal/scalar or another landed owner already gates (string bounds in CHARACTERS not bytes, uint53, digests, UUIDv7, timestamps, sorted-unique arrays, closed-shape decoding, the AX number model that forbids floating point, values at or beyond 2^53 and rounding-and-continuing). Delegate to it and keep only your package-specific rules. Every fork this epic produced became a defect: a byte-measured bound, an extension value rounded at 2^60, nested duplicate members collapsed by a lenient decode.\n16|(d) A census or an inventory standing in for behaviour. A reflection census of field NAMES does not prove that a cached observation cannot authorize; an arm inventory keyed by message text does not prove a condition edit is caught. Drive the input, assert the effect.\n17|(e) Mutant rows that do not measure what they claim. An arm-delete (`&& false`) is not a narrowing; a row patching two sites whose kill comes from one is one measured site reported as two; a plant with no raw log and no subprocess exit is a verdict line, not evidence. Ship one raw log per plant per run, state narrowing vs arm-delete per row, and include an applied harmless SURVIVED control so the harness is proven able to report a survivor.\n18|(f) Prose that outruns the tests. \"Composes X\", \"never admits what decoding refuses\", \"nothing re-implemented\", \"no cached sentinel can authorize\" are censusable claims: a reviewer greps for the callers and plants the counter-example. Before you write a sentence like that in a doc comment, README, LOGBOOK or TRACEABILITY row, make a test fail without the property. If you cannot, state it as an explicit BOUND instead, naming what is not covered.\n19|Finally: report the coverage ratio you MEASURED, not the one you planned. Two of the three rejected revisions claimed a complete ratio and the reviewer measured a smaller one; an honest smaller number with named gaps is accepted, an inflated one is a finding.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c3d3","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c5d0-c246-7b92-beac-dc3b11390997"},"sequence":68,"recorded_at":1780531400000131,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"aa3bb7a1-c12a-4660-a0d5-ffba7d41ef0c","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"aa3bb7a1-c12a-4660-a0d5-ffba7d41ef0c","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"aa3bb7a1-c12a-4660-a0d5-ffba7d41ef0c"},"call_id":"call_01a0c5d0f8167702a4bec6107356ff58","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-35urbp/TASK-260830-35urbp_reviewer-cr6.md`.\n1|Independently review Change Request revision 6 of TASK-260830-35urbp (implement-private-tmux-server-management), the FIRST of three leaves of STORY-260830-2t4g7i (production-tmux-backend; the chain is 35urbp -> 1c28dz -> g0pcnt). Change Request shape: task_delta on the Story branch (trunk base 799c338; checkpointed predecessors none; tip 799c338e401fca0b24859c0b870cd665927209f2), published by RUN-260921-a765d6 on muse-spark max, 23 changed paths, patch and validation log attached as TASK-260830-35urbp_change-request_rev6.patch / _rev6-validation.log. Revisions 1..5 are earlier construction attempts of the same producer scope that failed the Change Request validation suite on the pre-PR51 10m race-test timeout under concurrent suites; they carry no review verdict and no prior review findings — review revision 6 on its own merits.. Read the producer brief TASK-260830-35urbp_producer.md, the outcome TASK-260830-35urbp_results.md, TASK-260830-35urbp_conformance-matrix.md, TASK-260830-35urbp_producer-evidence.tar.gz, the CR patch and validation log, and the exact immutable CR bytes.\n2|\n3|NORMATIVE AUTHORITY: the pinned `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md` **§3.2** (lines 806-813, which fix the runtime root, the socket path `<runtime>/tmux/ax.sock` and its component-by-component custody) and **§4.2 tmux backend** (lines 1403-1449), with §4.C (1082), §4.D (1220), §4.E (1309) and §4.4 (1478-1490) as context. §3.2 was missing from the producer's authority list for revisions 1-3 and the rev3 review found the candidate diverging from it, so check it explicitly: the derived path, the identity of `Request.Root` as the Runtime IPC root rather than the durable state root, and whether any committed test pins the old literals and therefore defends a divergence. The task record's Scope still names v0.5.0 and that is stale — if the candidate cites a v0.5.0 line number or quotes text that is not in the pinned file, that is a finding. Derive every expectation from the spec text, never from a production constant.\n4|\n5|Verify with your own instruments, on isolated immutable copies of the exact candidate tree; never mutate the live Story worktree, index, branch or HEAD; no product edits, commits, checkpoints or integration.\n6|\n7|(1) **The dedicated-server rule, per vector.** \"AX MUST use its dedicated `-S` server and MUST NOT discover or reuse the operator's default tmux server by ambient socket name\" is not one gate. Drive each vector separately — an environment variable naming a socket, an inherited socket, a default path, a conventional name — and for each, assert the refusal at the production entry the matrix names. A candidate that closes one vector and reports the class is the single most likely shape here; census the call sites and plant a fresh spelling that walks through.\n8|\n9|(2) **The background-caller rules, which are the hard part.** A Background caller MUST NOT create a credential-dependent tmux server. A background CLI, SSH RPC process, daemon or restore worker MAY contact an already-running authenticated broker and its attested server, and if neither exists it MUST return `capability_unavailable` with typed realm/readiness details and MUST NOT fall back to direct server creation. Plant a direct-creation call on the background path and require a committed test to redden; a fall-back prohibition implemented as a comment, a doc line or an unreachable branch is a P1. Assert the LITERAL token `capability_unavailable` and the typed realm/readiness detail, not `== pkg.SomeConst` — swap the constant to another registered value with the same exit and see whether the suite notices.\n10|\n11|(3) **`launchctl managername` is a diagnostic hint only, and a cached sentinel or prior observation MUST NOT authorize.** This is exactly the shape that has been faked on this epic before with a reflection census of field names. Drive a cached/stale observation into the production entry and assert it authorizes nothing; a name census is not an effect census.\n12|\n13|(4) **Owner-only runtime directories.** Mode, ownership and containment are three gates. Check specifically that path logic delegates to the landed `internal/secprim` openat-relative walk rather than re-implementing containment: lexical containment plus `O_NOFOLLOW` is not containment, a symlinked intermediate escapes it, and a check after `open()` never runs on a FIFO. Plant a symlinked intermediate component and a FIFO.\n14|\n15|(5) **The determinism constraint, verified not read.** The brief required every rule to be driven to its effect by a committed test that passes with NO tmux process anywhere, with any real-tmux test separately gated and never the only witness for an acceptance row. Verify it by running the suite in an environment where tmux cannot be reached (make the binary unresolvable in your isolated copy) and reporting exactly which tests fail or skip. A row whose only witness skips in that run is an unmeasured row, however green the producer's log looks. Also check the converse: a rule degraded into a mock-only shape so it could be tested is a finding, not a solution — the production entry must still be the thing under test.\n16|\n17|(6) **No forked owners.** `internal/terminalbackend`, `internal/axpane`, `internal/terminstance`, `internal/termbind`, `internal/secprim`, `internal/environ`, `internal/canonicaljson`, `internal/scalar` are landed. Grep for a second model of anything they already own (string bounds in characters not bytes, uint53 and the AX number model, digests, sorted-unique arrays, closed-shape decoding, argv and path safety). The results must name which existing type or gate was extended; verify that claim rather than accepting it — \"composes X\" and \"nothing re-implemented\" are censusable claims.\n18|\n19|(7) **Traceability boundary.** This leaf must NOT touch `internal/traceability` (registry, digest pin, README measured-coverage subsection) — that belongs to the final leaf g0pcnt. Any edit there is a finding. Package-local TRACEABILITY.md and the conformance matrix are the right places.\n20|\n21|(8) **Mutation and hygiene.** Rerun the shipped harness in an isolated copy, rerun each KILLED twice, and plant at least four narrowing mutants of your own on gates the producer did not mutate, plus an applied harmless SURVIVED control. Per-plant raw logs, subprocess exits, precise denominators; NOT_APPLIED is not a pass. `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`; zero `__pycache__`/`.pyc` in the CR tree or your copies. gofmt/vet clean. The candidate must be byte-identical to trunk everywhere outside this leaf's scope — check every path in `git diff --name-only <the CR base> <current origin/main>` that also appears in the candidate, because a refresh carries stale pre-refresh copies that read as reverts. Crash and idempotency evidence is required for every durable write (a runtime directory and a server socket are durable writes) or an explicit purity bound. The full configured suite must be green on the exact tree; read the command count from the candidate config rather than assuming a number.\n22|\n23|Report the coverage ratio YOU measured against the acceptance table's real row count, not the producer's restated one. Attach TASK-260830-35urbp_review-verdict-rev6.md and TASK-260830-35urbp_review-evidence-rev6.tar.gz (a real gzip archive), complete the live merged checklist, then `accept_cr(TASK-260830-35urbp, revision=6, evidence=TASK-260830-35urbp_review-verdict-rev6.md)` or hand off changes requested with P1/P2/P3 classes named and a short \"Rework scope (for the producer)\" section at the end. Model: claude-opus-5 max. Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c3d5","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c5d0-c246-7b92-beac-dc3b11390997"},"sequence":69,"recorded_at":1780531400000133,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"aa3bb7a1-c12a-4660-a0d5-ffba7d41ef0c","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"aa3bb7a1-c12a-4660-a0d5-ffba7d41ef0c","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"aa3bb7a1-c12a-4660-a0d5-ffba7d41ef0c"},"call_id":"call_01a0c5d0fb3277d0835cb19f629647bb","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-35urbp/TASK-260830-35urbp_producer.md`.\n1|Implement TASK-260830-35urbp (implement-private-tmux-server-management), the FIRST of three leaves of STORY-260830-2t4g7i (production-tmux-backend). The chain is 35urbp -> TASK-260830-1c28dz (tmux lifecycle operations) -> TASK-260830-g0pcnt (generation and attach semantics, the final leaf). You own only this leaf.\n2|\n3|AUTHORITY. The task record's Scope names the spec at v0.5.0. That reference is STALE: this repository adopted v0.7.0 (STORY-260917-110onn, landed) and the pinned copy is `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md`. Your normative authority is its **§4.2 tmux backend** (lines 1403-1449), with **§4.C Lifecycle and operations** (1082), **§4.D Closed capabilities and evidence** (1220) and **§4.E Persistence, transport, security, and compatibility** (1309) as its context. Quote the pinned file, never the network, and never a v0.5.0 line number.\n4|\n5|WHAT THIS LEAF MUST DELIVER. Owner-only runtime directories and dedicated `tmux -S` server management, provably without ambient or default-server discovery or reuse. The normative rules you are implementing, in the spec's own words:\n6|1. AX MUST use its dedicated `-S` server and MUST NOT discover or reuse the operator's default tmux server by ambient socket name. \"By ambient socket name\" is the measurable part: an environment variable, an inherited socket, a default path and a conventional name are four separate vectors and each needs its own refusal row.\n7|2. On macOS, server creation is credential-sensitive. A Background caller MUST NOT create a credential-dependent tmux server.\n8|3. A background CLI, SSH RPC process, daemon, or restore worker MAY contact an already-running authenticated Aqua broker and its attested AX tmux server; if neither exists it MUST return `capability_unavailable` with typed realm/readiness details and MUST NOT fall back to direct server creation. The fall-back prohibition is the rule most likely to be implemented as a comment rather than as a gate — a reviewer will plant a direct-creation call on the background path and expect a committed test to redden.\n9|4. `launchctl managername` is a diagnostic hint ONLY. A cached sentinel or a prior `managername` observation MUST NOT authorize anything. If you expose any readiness fact, make its non-authorizing character a driven test, not a sentence.\n10|5. Runtime directories are owner-only. Treat the mode, the ownership and the containment of that directory as three separate gates, and remember the landed lesson that lexical containment plus `O_NOFOLLOW` is NOT containment: check `internal/secprim` and the openat-relative walk that already exists before writing any path logic of your own.\n11|\n12|DETERMINISM IS A HARD CONSTRAINT, AND IT SHAPES THE DESIGN. AGENTS.md requires tests that are deterministic and free of network or terminal dependencies. tmux 3.6a happens to be installed on this host; that is NOT a licence to depend on it. Requirement: every rule above must be driven to its effect by a committed test that passes with no tmux process anywhere. If you also write a test that talks to a real tmux server, it must be separately gated and it must NOT be the only witness for any acceptance row — state in the results which rows, if any, have a real-tmux witness in addition to their deterministic one. How you achieve that is your design decision; do not ask, and do not degrade a rule into a mock-only shape to make it testable. If a rule genuinely cannot be driven without a live server, say so as an explicit BOUND with the reason, rather than pretending.\n13|\n14|DO NOT FORK A LANDED OWNER. This repository already carries `internal/terminalbackend` (18.6k lines), `internal/axpane` (8.8k), `internal/terminstance` (7.1k) and `internal/termbind` (4.5k), plus `internal/secprim`/`internal/secconftest` for path and argv safety, `internal/environ` for environment handling, `internal/canonicaljson` and `internal/scalar` for closed shapes and the AX number model. Read them BEFORE you write a type. Your predecessor dependency TASK-260830-2056mm landed in STORY-260830-ptxkqe (PR #55) — read `TASK-260830-2056mm_results.md` and its accepted verdict, because the pane/terminal-instance binding it delivered is what your server management has to sit under. Say in the results which existing type or gate you extended and which you deliberately did not. Every fork this epic produced became a defect.\n15|\n16|TRACEABILITY. Do NOT edit `internal/traceability` (ownership registry, digest pin, README measured-coverage subsection) in this leaf — the Story's FINAL leaf (g0pcnt) carries the registry bindings and the re-pin. Document your clause coverage in a package-local TRACEABILITY.md and in the conformance matrix instead.\n17|\n18|EVIDENCE CONTRACT (repository DoD). Every AC row driven through a production entry by a named committed test with a stated n-of-m ratio and call sites; a negative for every refusal, asserting the literal spec token (`capability_unavailable`) and the typed realm/readiness detail, not a production constant; a narrowing mutant per gate executed by a shipped harness with per-plant raw logs, subprocess exits and an applied harmless SURVIVED control (`PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`, no `__pycache__` anywhere); crash and idempotency evidence for every durable write — creating a runtime directory and a server socket IS a durable write, so the landed no-replace + fsync + hooks + real-kill pattern applies, or state an explicit purity bound; a conformance matrix mapping each pinned clause to a test or a stated bound; a README package section with test commands and NO capability or CLI claim (no `ax` command exists yet); a LOGBOOK entry, newest-first.\n19|\n20|WORKSPACE. This is the FIRST leaf, so the managed Story worktree does not exist yet — the spawn provisions `.temp/STORY-260830-2t4g7i/worktree` on branch `task-board/story/STORY-260830-2t4g7i` forked from trunk `799c338`. Your candidate is the UNCOMMITTED working tree there: exactly one leaf's worth of delta. Never commit on the Story branch, never edit `.task-board` directly, never self-accept. If origin/main moves before your handoff run `task-board worktree refresh-candidate TASK-260830-35urbp`, then audit every path in `git diff --name-only <old-base> <new-base>` that also appears in your `git status` and restore trunk content by hand — a refresh carries stale pre-refresh copies of trunk-changed files into the candidate and they read as reverts. Before handoff `git status` shows only candidate paths.\n21|\n22|PROCESS. Read the Curator-managed `go-testing-tools` skill first. All CI is local; never trigger hosted CI. Run your own package tests and the harness BEFORE handoff, then the full configured validation suite once — read the command count from the candidate's `task-board.config.json` (it is 30 at trunk 799c338, not 27); command 5 is `go test ./... -race -count=1 -timeout 25m` and can take 25-40 minutes under concurrent runs, which is expected and must not be shortened. Report the coverage ratio you MEASURED. Hand off no later than 3.5 hours in; if the full scope cannot be finished, hand off a reviewable slice with the remaining items enumerated precisely in the results. Attach TASK-260830-35urbp_results.md, TASK-260830-35urbp_conformance-matrix.md and TASK-260830-35urbp_producer-evidence.tar.gz (a real gzip archive), keep the checklist current, then `task-board handoff TASK-260830-35urbp --role developer` and exit promptly. Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board. Model: muse-spark max. The independent reviewer will be claude-opus-5 max.\n23|REJECTION PATTERNS THE INDEPENDENT REVIEWER HAS ALREADY CAUGHT ON THIS EPIC (2026-09-17: TASK-260830-1geqhj rev1, TASK-260830-24z2b3 rev2, TASK-260830-219okr rev3 were all routed CHANGES REQUESTED, and between them these six shapes account for every finding). Read this as a checklist you run against your own work BEFORE handoff; each item names what a reviewer will do to your candidate.\n24|(a) Circular expectations. An assertion that compares a production value against a production constant (`got.Code == pkg.SomeUnsupportedCode`) pins nothing: swapping the constant to another registered value with the same exit keeps the suite green. Assert the LITERAL token from the pinned specification text, at the production entry, and make sure the literal actually occurs in a committed test — not only in a comment. Derive every expectation from the spec, never from the implementation.\n25|(b) A rule pinned at the helper instead of the entry. A test that calls the inner helper directly proves the helper; it says nothing about whether the composed production entry still reaches it. Drive every rule through the entry point the conformance matrix names as its call site, and if a rule is implemented TWICE (a Build path and a Decode path, an exported entry and its internal sibling), each side needs its own narrowing mutant — a rule pinned only on one side leaves the other side unmeasured, and reviewers plant exactly there.\n26|(c) Forking a landed gate. Never re-implement what internal/environ, internal/canonicaljson, internal/scalar or another landed owner already gates (string bounds in CHARACTERS not bytes, uint53, digests, UUIDv7, timestamps, sorted-unique arrays, closed-shape decoding, the AX number model that forbids floating point, values at or beyond 2^53 and rounding-and-continuing). Delegate to it and keep only your package-specific rules. Every fork this epic produced became a defect: a byte-measured bound, an extension value rounded at 2^60, nested duplicate members collapsed by a lenient decode.\n27|(d) A census or an inventory standing in for behaviour. A reflection census of field NAMES does not prove that a cached observation cannot authorize; an arm inventory keyed by message text does not prove a condition edit is caught. Drive the input, assert the effect.\n28|(e) Mutant rows that do not measure what they claim. An arm-delete (`&& false`) is not a narrowing; a row patching two sites whose kill comes from one is one measured site reported as two; a plant with no raw log and no subprocess exit is a verdict line, not evidence. Ship one raw log per plant per run, state narrowing vs arm-delete per row, and include an applied harmless SURVIVED control so the harness is proven able to report a survivor.\n29|(f) Prose that outruns the tests. \"Composes X\", \"never admits what decoding refuses\", \"nothing re-implemented\", \"no cached sentinel can authorize\" are censusable claims: a reviewer greps for the callers and plants the counter-example. Before you write a sentence like that in a doc comment, README, LOGBOOK or TRACEABILITY row, make a test fail without the property. If you cannot, state it as an explicit BOUND instead, naming what is not covered.\n30|Finally: report the coverage ratio you MEASURED, not the one you planned. Two of the three rejected revisions claimed a complete ratio and the reviewer measured a smaller one; an honest smaller number with named gaps is accepted, an inflated one is a finding.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
