ctor` or capability claim; LOGBOOK newest-first with the rev6 block; crash evidence real (`TestEnsureCrashChildSelfTerminates` SIGKILLs the child inside `AfterMkdir` and proves retry convergence) and idempotency evidence present (`TestEnsureRuntimeDirIsIdempotent`, `TestAcquireCreatesRuntimeDirIdempotently`, `TestAcquireForegroundSpawnIsIdempotentAcrossRetry`); the server socket's own crash evidence is B9 (lifecycle leaf) | `logs/static-gates.log` |\n53|\n54|## Closure of the rev5 findings (verified by driving, not by reading the results table)\n55|\n56|| rev5 | Closed? | How verified |\n57|| --- | --- | --- |\n58|| P2-A four members: zero admission (R09), admitted-without-generation (R10), decoy-only (R19), fallback via `acquireForeground` guarded on `ProbeServer` (R18) | **yes** | R09 shape shipped as `N-broker-zero-admission`, KILLED ×2 by the `zero_server_admission` subtests in both `TestAcquireBackgroundMissReturnsTypedUnavailable` and `TestCheckBrokerContactRefusesEachMissingFact`; the R10 and R19 shapes re-planted by this reviewer as R02/R03 against the FULL suite → KILLED ×2 by `admitted_server_without_generation` / `decoy-only_server_admission` in both tables (the producer's anchor-share replay claim reproduces); R18 shipped as `D-background-fallback-foreground`, KILLED ×2 by every miss subtest plus the Linux miss; `ProbeServer` spy armed in 23/23 (mechanical, reproduced) and the effect census reddens all 16 tests that enter the function; row 31 and README now say both foreground dependencies |\n59|| P3-A ownership member of the absence class | **yes** | `TestAcquireBackgroundStagesOwnershipRefusal` (unix file, `effectiveUID` seam) exists and passes; `N-absence-remap-ownership` KILLED ×2 with the top-level-type kill line; sibling rows `N-absence-remap-containment`/`-invalid` KILLED ×2 |\n60|| P3-B false \"before any side effect\" | **yes** | `acquireForeground` parses the session before `EnsureRuntimeDir` and the probe; `TestAcquireForegroundRefusesMalformedSession` asserts no probe, no spawn, no directory; `N-session-entry` KILLED ×2 by `server was probed before a malformed session refused`; the acquire.go:142-147 sentence now enumerates the members that are true and I could not find a member it overstates (root grammar, override, collision, details, dependencies, session all refuse before the directory on the foreground path; reviewer rows R11/R12 confirm the verify-before-probe and ensure-before-probe orderings are pinned) |\n61|| Obs 1-6 | **yes** | row 23 comma-root text; B16 \"symlinked or relative alias\"; B9 `Dependencies.Spawn` inert; B15 names the commit-side leaf-Stat and NewGuard arms; `TestAcquireBackgroundInvalidGenerationRefusesAfterProbe` + `N-details-constructor` KILLED ×2; `static-gates.log` carries exits |\n62|\n63|## P2 — must fix or record as a reviewed decision\n64|\n65|### P2-A. The commit-side non-directory-leaf gate (`O_DIRECTORY` on the commit `Openat`, runtime_unix.go:58-59) has no narrowing row, its admit direction is unmeasured, and its no-hang property is unmeasured — the census rowed the verify side only\n66|\n67|SPEC §3.2 810-812: before bind AX MUST reject a socket path, parent or ancestor \"whose file kind\n68|… [is] unsafe\"; row 5 claims \"Non-directory leaf refuses on commit and verify … FIFO refusal\n69|relies on O_DIRECTORY failing fast, pinned by the deadline test\". The candidate implements the\n70|gate correctly on both sides (same flags on both `Openat` calls), and production refuses a 0700\n71|regular file and a FIFO on the commit side without blocking (probes K01/K01b/K01c pass on the\n72|untouched candidate). What is not true is the measurement claim:\n73|\n74|| Row | Plant (runtime_unix.go) | Committed suite | With probe | What the committed suite does not see |\n75|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n76|| R01 | drop `unix.O_DIRECTORY` from the COMMIT `Openat` (the exact twin of the producer's `N-containment-odirectory-verify`, which drops it from the verify `Openat`) | KILLED ×2 **by reroute only**: `TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesNonDirectoryLeaf` fails with `err = tmux_unsafe_runtime_dir at runtime mode, want … at runtime containment` — its fixture is a 0600 file, so the mode gate catches what the containment gate no longer does; `TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesSymlinkLeaf`, the crash test and every other commit test stay green | K01 kills (`EnsureRuntimeDir` on a 0700 regular file: `err = nil`); K01c kills (foreground `Acquire` on the same leaf: `err = nil` — the entry admits the leaf, probes the server and spawns into `<root>/tmux/ax.sock` where `tmux` is a regular file); K01b kills (`EnsureRuntimeDir` on a FIFO leaf **BLOCKED for 5s** — the writer-less `O_RDONLY` open stalls) | a 0700 non-directory leaf is ADMITTED on `EnsureRuntimeDir` and through the foreground entry; a FIFO leaf HANGS the creating path |\n77|\n78|Why this is a P2 and not a P3: the verify side was given exactly this treatment in rev3 (the\n79|`TestVerifyRuntimeDirRefusesNonDirectoryLeaf` comment says the regular file \"carries 0700 so a\n80|weakened open admits it outright instead of rerouting to the mode gate\", and the FIFO subtest runs\n81|\"under a deadline so the no-hang property is pinned too\"), and the shipped row's own note asserts\n82|\"the commit side still refuses\" without a fixture that could tell. The rule is implemented twice\n83|(commit and verify), rejection pattern (b) as stated in every brief of this task requires a\n84|narrowing per side, and the harness has 3 verify-side containment rows (`-symlink-verify`,\n85|`-odirectory-verify`, `N-root-symlink-verify`) against 2 commit-side (`-symlink`,\n86|`N-root-symlink-commit`) — the O_DIRECTORY commit row is the missing one. The census cell\n87|`commit (runtime_unix.go:35) × ENS` lists ten rows and none of them touches this arm, while the\n88|`verify × VER` cell lists `N-containment-odirectory-verify` explicitly: the instrument that was\n89|this round's deliverable shows the asymmetry and did not flag it. The DoD line \"Every gate ships\n90|at least one NARROWING mutant … and a named test must fail\" is unmet for this arm (a test fails,\n91|but for the mode gate's reason, and the DoD item is unchecked below for that reason). Production\n92|is correct today; the fix is tests plus a row:\n93|\n94|1. give the commit side the verify side's fixtures — a 0700 regular-file leaf on\n95|   `EnsureRuntimeDir` and through foreground `Acquire` (K01/K01c are the templates; assert no\n96|   probe and no spawn), and a FIFO leaf on `EnsureRuntimeDir` under the existing\n97|   `verifyWithDeadline` (K01b);\n98|2. ship `N-containment-odirectory-commit` (the R01 shape), name it under row 5 and in the\n99|   `commit × ENS` and `commit × AFG` census cells, and reword the row-5 FIFO clause to name both\n100|   deadline tests;\n101|3. correct the `N-containment-odirectory-verify` note (\"the commit side still refuses\") to point\n102|   at the new commit row rather than asserting it.\n103|\n104|## P3 — fix in the same rework\n105|\n106|- **P3-A. The no-fallback rule's platform axis is pinned at the miss arm for macOS and Linux only.**\n107|  Reviewer row R16 (a fallback `Spawn` on the background MISS path guarded on\n108|  `req.Platform == scalar.PlatformWSL2`) **SURVIVED ×2** the full suite: the miss tables drive\n109|  macOS (8 shapes) and Linux (1 shape, row 29), and the only WSL2 background test\n110|  (`TestAcquireBackgroundVerifiesWithoutCreating/wsl2`) refuses on the absent leaf before the miss\n111|  arm, so no committed test reaches a WSL2 miss. The sibling narrowings are pinned — R15 (the\n112|  same guard on Linux) KILLED ×2 by `TestAcquireBackgroundMissOnLinuxAlsoRefusesWithoutFallback`,\n113|  R17 (WSL2 background callers dispatched to the foreground path) KILLED ×2 by\n114|  `…VerifiesWithoutCreating/wsl2`, R27 (absence remap withheld on WSL2) KILLED ×2 — so this is one\n115|  member, not a class. Probe K16 (WSL2 miss with a live leaf, spy spawner + spy probe →\n116|  `capability_unavailable`, spawn 0) passes on the candidate and kills R16 (`spawn calls = 1, want\n117|  0 on a WSL2 miss`). This is the same shape as rev4 P3-A (absence remap pinned on macOS only),\n118|  one arm over. Fix: make the Linux miss test a platform table `{linux, wsl2}` (or add a WSL2\n119|  subtest to the miss table), add it to `BG_MISS_LINUX` so `N-creation-literal` and both `D-` rows\n120|  kill through all three tmux platforms, and name it under rows 29/31.\n121|- **P3-B. The attestation membership arm is pinned for one decoy of the sixteen-value §4.D\n122|  vocabulary.** Reviewer row R07 (`CheckServerAttested` admits `Has(\"local_attach\")` alongside\n123|  the realm row) **SURVIVED ×2**: every committed decoy is `headless_creation`\n124|  (`fixtureDecoyCapacity`), so a narrowing keyed on any of the other fourteen non-realm\n125|  capabilities walks through the helper, the broker contact and both `Acquire` paths. Probe K07\n126|  (`local_attach`-only admission at the helper and through the background miss →\n127|  `server attestation` / `capability_unavailable`, spawn 0) passes on the candidate and kills R07.\n128|  The independent source exists in the tree — `catalog.Current().Capabilities` is the exact\n129|  sixteen-value Section 4.D table — so the completeness shape from `negative-evidence.md` applies:\n130|  derive the decoy set from the catalog, assert every non-realm capability alone (and all of them\n131|  together without the realm row) refuses at the helper and through the background entry, and let\n132|  the existing `N-realm-membership` row keep its `headless_creation` member while the new test\n133|  closes the other fourteen. Production is correct (`Has` is exact-match); this is measurement.\n134|\n135|## Observations (not findings; a sentence each if the producer agrees)\n136|\n137|1. Bound B9 witnessed as stated: R06 (a direct `os/exec` `tmux -S <socket> new-session -d` call\n138|   planted on the background miss path, error discarded) **SURVIVED ×2** with tmux unresolvable —\n139|   the no-fallback proof covers `Dependencies.Spawn` and the `acquireForeground` re-entry and\n140|   excludes a direct exec only by the import census, exactly as B9 says. Honest; no change asked.\n141|   (Do not run that plant on a host with tmux on PATH: it would create a real server in the test's\n142|   temp root.)\n143|2. `TestEnsureCrashChildSelfTerminates` flaked once in ~35 full-suite runs under host load 12-14\n144|   (`child status = exit status 1, want killed by SIGKILL`, in the first R28 run; 25 isolated\n145|   runs, 6 full-suite runs on the untouched candidate and 3 R28 reruns all PASS). The parent\n146|   discards the child's stdout/stderr (`child.Run()` with neither set), so the exit-1 cause is\n147|   undiagnosable from the log. Capturing the child's combined output into the failure message\n148|   costs two lines and would make the next occurrence attributable.\n149|3. `TestBuildArgvRefusesInvalidArgvShape` is the one committed top-level test not named in\n150|   TRACEABILITY.md (B12 describes the arm without naming its witness); the conformance matrix\n151|   lists row number 46 twice (two clauses under one number).\n152|4. The `argv × AFG` census cell names the socket and session arms as U3 but not the\n153|   `secprim.CheckArgv` shape arm, which through `Acquire` is B12 (unreachable: root is\n154|   `ParseAbsolutePath`-valid, leaf fixed, session pre-parsed); worth naming B12 in the cell.\n155|5. `N-details-constructor`'s note says the mutant \"reports success with a zero outcome and no\n156|   error\"; the raw log shows it returns a typed-nil `*axerror.Error` inside a non-nil `error`\n157|   (`err top-level type = *axerror.Error (<nil>)`). Killed either way; the note is wrong about the\n158|   mechanism.\n159|6. B11 witnessed as stated (P11): a symlinked INTERMEDIATE component of the runtime root is\n160|   followed on both entries. This is the same bound as the landed `secprim.OpenNoFollowDir` root\n161|   open and is design-necessary on macOS, where `localstore` resolves the Runtime IPC root under\n162|   `$TMPDIR` (`/var/folders/…`, and `/var` is itself a symlink), so a strict no-follow walk from\n163|   `/` could never admit the platform default. Not a finding.\n164|\n165|## §M — reviewer battery (17 rows + 4 extra rows, two passes, `battery/reviewer_battery.py`)\n166|\n167|Every row: anchor count verified (all applied, none NOT_APPLIED, none COMPILE_FAIL), plant applied\n168|to the mutant copy from the pristine candidate bytes, the committed suite run as shipped (full\n169|package, `-count=1 -v`, **no `-run` mask** — unlike the producer harness, which scopes each row),\n170|exit + raw output logged with an `exit:` header, file restored from the pristine copy and\n171|re-compared, package directory hash equal before/after (`e0314ddb4b26dfda`), `internal/` re-diffed\n172|against the candidate copy after each pass. Rows predicted SURVIVED were additionally run with\n173|`zz_review_probe_test.go` present and `-run TestReview…` (`battery/pass1-probe/`).\n174|\n175|| Row | Kind | Gate (site) | Committed suite | With probe | Killer(s) |\n176|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n177|| R01-commit-odirectory-drop | narrowing (flag) | commit-side non-directory leaf (runtime_unix.go:59) | KILLED **by reroute only** (`runtime mode` ≠ `runtime containment`) | KILLED | K01, K01b (5s BLOCK), K01c (P2-A) |\n178|| R02-broker-admitted-without-generation | narrowing | broker-side server wiring (readiness.go:86), rev5 R10 shape | KILLED | — | `…MissReturnsTypedUnavailable/admitted_server_without_generation`, `…BrokerContactRefusesEachMissingFact/admitted_server_without_generation` |\n179|| R03-broker-decoy-only-admits | narrowing | same site, rev5 R19 shape | KILLED | — | the two `decoy-only_server_admission` subtests |\n180|| R04-unavailable-code-swap-same-exit | narrowing (token) | `backgroundUnavailable` emits `terminal_backend_capability_unproven` (exit 6, registered 1.3.0) with the same typed details (acquire.go:297) | KILLED | — | every miss subtest + Linux miss + `…VerifiesWithoutCreating` ×3: `code = \"terminal_backend_capability_unproven\", want \"capability_unavailable\"` |\n181|| R05-detail-swap-generation | narrowing (detail) | `TmuxServerGeneration` carries `BrokerState` (acquire.go:294) | KILLED | — | every unavailable-asserting test: `detail \"tmux_server_generation\" = absent, want \"generation-7\"` |\n182|| R06-exec-fallback-B9-witness | additive (bound) | direct `os/exec` spawn on the background miss (acquire.go:204) | **SURVIVED** | — | (stated bound B9; observation 1) |\n183|| R07-membership-fresh-decoy-local-attach | narrowing | membership arm admits `local_attach` (readiness.go:40) | **SURVIVED** | KILLED | K07 (P3-B) |\n184|| R08-verify-odirectory-drop-replay | replay | producer `N-containment-odirectory-verify` against the full suite | KILLED | — | `TestVerifyRuntimeDirRefusesNonDirectoryLeaf/{regular_file,fifo_without_blocking}` (5s BLOCK), `TestAcquireBackgroundRefusesNonDirectoryLeaf` |\n185|| R11-background-probe-before-verify | order | broker probed before custody (acquire.go:183-193) | KILLED (8 top-level tests) | — | `…VerifiesWithoutCreating` ×3 (\"broker was probed for an absent runtime directory\"), every background custody test (\"broker was probed past …\") |\n186|| R12-foreground-probe-before-ensure | order | server probed before ensure (acquire.go:228-235) | KILLED | — | `…StagesCommitPhaseCustodyRefusal`, `…RefusesBadRoot/missing` |\n187|| R15-linux-only-fallback-spawn | additive (platform-narrowed) | fallback spawn on a Linux miss (acquire.go:204) | KILLED | — | `TestAcquireBackgroundMissOnLinuxAlsoRefusesWithoutFallback` |\n188|| R16-wsl2-only-fallback-spawn | additive (platform-narrowed) | fallback spawn on a WSL2 miss (acquire.go:204) | **SURVIVED** | KILLED | K16 (P3-A) |\n189|| R17-dispatch-wsl2-background-to-foreground | narrowing | dispatch (acquire.go:163) routes WSL2 background callers foreground | KILLED | — | `…VerifiesWithoutCreating/wsl2` (directory created, spawn 1) |\n190|| R22-collision-skipped-for-background | narrowing (caller axis) | collision gate bypassed for background at the entry (acquire.go:159) | KILLED | — | `TestAcquireRefusesAmbientCollision/*/background` ×5, unclean + TMUX-encoding background legs |\n191|| R23-override-skipped-for-background | narrowing (caller axis) | override gate bypassed for background at the entry (acquire.go:159) | KILLED | — | `TestAcquireRefusesEveryAmbientOverrideVector/*/background` ×6 |\n192|| C-reviewer-control | control | comment-only edit in acquire.go | SURVIVED | — | (must survive; proves the battery observes outcomes) |\n193|| R25-realm-constant-swap-headless | narrowing (token) | `realmCapability` swapped to another registered §4.D value | KILLED | — | every unavailable test (`detail \"capability\"` literal), `…ForegroundRefusesRunningUnattested` (decoy attaches), `…BackgroundContactsBroker` |\n194|| R26-principal-generation-admits-when-server-bound | narrowing | principal-generation arm waived for an attested server (readiness.go:83) | KILLED | — | `generation-unbound_principal` in both tables, `empty_principal_generation`, `both_generations_empty` |\n195|| R27-absence-remap-withheld-on-wsl2 | narrowing | absence remap (acquire.go:184) skipped for WSL2 | KILLED | — | `…VerifiesWithoutCreating/wsl2` |\n196|| R28-effect-census-probe-at-background-top | effect census | guarded `ProbeServer` call at the top of `acquireBackground` | KILLED (16 top-level tests; +1 crash-test flake in run 1 only, observation 2) | — | every background test that enters the function |\n197|\n198|Denominator: 21 applied rows = 12 narrowing + 3 additive + 1 replay + 2 order + 1 effect census\n199|+ 1 control (+ R28 counted once). Of the 12 narrowings, 10 KILLED by the committed suite, 2\n200|SURVIVED (R07 outright; R01 killed only by reroute, admit direction and no-hang unmeasured) —\n201|each proven real by a probe kill (production correct, suite blind). Of the 3 additives, R15 KILLED,\n202|R16 SURVIVED (probe kill), R06 SURVIVED as the stated bound. Replay, both orderings and the effect\n203|census KILLED. Every KILLED row was killed by exactly the tests named above (kill lines in the raw\n204|logs). Passes 1 and 2 identical.\n205|\n206|## §P — reviewer probes (7, `logs/probes-rev6-baseline.log`, all PASS on the untouched candidate)\n207|\n208|K01 `EnsureRuntimeDir` on a 0700 regular-file leaf → `runtime containment` (baseline for R01);\n209|K01b `EnsureRuntimeDir` on a FIFO leaf under a 5s deadline → `runtime containment` immediately;\n210|K01c foreground `Acquire` on the 0700 regular-file leaf → `runtime containment`, no probe, no\n211|spawn; K07 `local_attach`-only admission → `server attestation` at the helper and\n212|`capability_unavailable` through the background miss, spawn 0 (baseline for R07); K16 WSL2\n213|background miss with a present leaf → `capability_unavailable`, spawn 0, probe silent (baseline\n214|for R16); P11 symlinked intermediate root component followed on Ensure and Verify (B11 witness);\n215|P-FIFO FIFO leaf through the background entry → `runtime containment` fast, broker not probed.\n216|\n217|## What held under attack (keep)\n218|\n219|- Dedicated-server rule per vector: override refused on all five members plus whitespace on both\n220|  callers through `Acquire`, and the caller axis of both the override and the collision gate is\n221|  pinned at the entry (R22/R23 KILLED); the socket has exactly one constructor (`SocketPath`,\n222|  called from `ResolveSocket` and `BuildArgv`), one resolution site (`Acquire` → `ResolveSocket`)\n223|  and one spawn site; `Acquire` never reads the environment or execs; the §3.2 path is pinned at\n224|  the entry on both callers and at all three `RuntimeDirName` sites; the argv vector is pinned\n225|  element-by-element at the helper and through the entry.\n226|- Background rules: broker-or-refuse with the literal `capability_unavailable`, exit 6 and the\n227|  five typed details asserted as literals — a same-exit registered code swap (R04), a detail swap\n228|  (R05) and a realm-constant swap (R25) all redden; the broker-side attested-server conjunct is now\n229|  pinned for five admission shapes at the helper AND through the background entry (R02/R03\n230|  KILLED); the principal arms are pinned (R26); the absent-leaf cold state returns the typed\n231|  refusal on macOS, Linux and WSL2 (R27); the fallback is killed through `Spawn`, through\n232|  `acquireForeground` re-entry, on Linux (R15) and at the WSL2 dispatch (R17); custody precedes\n233|  the broker probe (R11) and ensure precedes the server probe (R12). Residue: P3-A.\n234|- Attestation / cached observations: no input exists for a managername hint or a cached sentinel\n235|  (`Request` and `RealmAdmission` have no such member); a replayed observation is a\n236|  stale-generation admission and refuses on both paths; the generation-binding and membership\n237|  arms are pinned at the helper, the broker contact and both entries (the producer's\n238|  `N-realm-membership`/`N-realm-generation` kill through four tables). Residue: P3-B.\n239|- Custody: mode (exact 0700, both sides, both directions), ownership (both sides, and the\n240|  absence classifier's ownership member at the background entry), containment on the verify side\n241|  (FIFO fast-fail, 0700 regular file, symlink leaf, symlink root, handle mismatch) and the\n242|  commit-side symlink leaf/root and mismatch all pinned; the top-level custody oracle sees the\n243|  wrapper; the real-SIGKILL crash test converges. Residue: P2-A (commit-side O_DIRECTORY arm).\n244|- Determinism: 0 SKIP with tmux unresolvable, 190 RUN; no real-tmux witness (B1); no mock-only\n245|  degradation.\n246|- Boundary: `internal/traceability` untouched; README section carries no CLI/capability claim; no\n247|  trunk drift; producer evidence archive complete and digest-verified; LOGBOOK newest-first.\n248|\n249|## Coverage ratio measured against the 58-row table\n250|\n251|**58 of 58 rows are driven as their statements are written**; the ratio is not inflated. The gaps\n252|sit beside the statements, at the member level: row 5 (the commit-side non-directory clause is\n253|driven for a 0600 file, i.e. by the mode gate, and its FIFO clause names one deadline test on one\n254|side — P2-A), rows 29/31 (the miss arm and the no-fallback census cover two of the three tmux\n255|platforms — P3-A), rows 35/27 (one decoy of fourteen — P3-B). Census: 50 of 264 cells measured\n256|as claimed; the `commit × ENS/AFG` cells are the ones whose row lists omit a live arm.\n257|\n258|## Rework scope (for the producer)\n259|\n260|1. **P2-A (tests + row + three sentences, no production change)**: mirror the verify-side\n261|   fixtures on the commit side — 0700 regular-file leaf on `EnsureRuntimeDir` and through\n262|   foreground `Acquire` (assert no probe, no spawn), FIFO leaf on `EnsureRuntimeDir` under\n263|   `verifyWithDeadline` (K01/K01b/K01c in the reviewer probe file are the templates); ship\n264|   `N-containment-odirectory-commit` (drop `O_DIRECTORY` from the commit `Openat`), name it under\n265|   row 5 and in the `commit × ENS` and `commit × AFG` census cells; reword row 5's FIFO clause to\n266|   both deadline tests; fix the `N-containment-odirectory-verify` note.\n267|2. **P3-A**: WSL2 member of the miss table (platform table on the Linux miss test or a WSL2\n268|   subtest), added to `BG_MISS_LINUX` so `N-creation-literal` and both `D-` rows kill on all three\n269|   platforms; name under rows 29/31.\n270|3. **P3-B**: a catalog-derived decoy completeness test (every non-realm `catalog.Current().Capabilities`\n271|   member alone, and all together, refuses at `CheckServerAttested` and through the background\n272|   miss); name under rows 27/35.\n273|4. Optional: capture the crash child's combined output in the failure message; name\n274|   `TestBuildArgvRefusesInvalidArgvShape` under B12; de-duplicate matrix row 46; B12 in the\n275|   `argv × AFG` cell; correct the `N-details-constructor` note.\n276|5. Rerun the package suite (tmux hidden), `GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go vet ./...`, the harness\n277|   twice, and the 30-command suite; refresh results/matrix/archive; hand off as revision 7.\n278|   Everything in \"What held under attack\" needs no change — do not re-litigate it.","final_result":true}}}
