link), so a strict no-follow walk from\n163|   `/` could never admit the platform default. Not a finding.\n164|\n165|## §M — reviewer battery (17 rows + 4 extra rows, two passes, `battery/reviewer_battery.py`)\n166|\n167|Every row: anchor count verified (all applied, none NOT_APPLIED, none COMPILE_FAIL), plant applied\n168|to the mutant copy from the pristine candidate bytes, the committed suite run as shipped (full\n169|package, `-count=1 -v`, **no `-run` mask** — unlike the producer harness, which scopes each row),\n170|exit + raw output logged with an `exit:` header, file restored from the pristine copy and\n171|re-compared, package directory hash equal before/after (`e0314ddb4b26dfda`), `internal/` re-diffed\n172|against the candidate copy after each pass. Rows predicted SURVIVED were additionally run with\n173|`zz_review_probe_test.go` present and `-run TestReview…` (`battery/pass1-probe/`).\n174|\n175|| Row | Kind | Gate (site) | Committed suite | With probe | Killer(s) |\n176|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n177|| R01-commit-odirectory-drop | narrowing (flag) | commit-side non-directory leaf (runtime_unix.go:59) | KILLED **by reroute only** (`runtime mode` ≠ `runtime containment`) | KILLED | K01, K01b (5s BLOCK), K01c (P2-A) |\n178|| R02-broker-admitted-without-generation | narrowing | broker-side server wiring (readiness.go:86), rev5 R10 shape | KILLED | — | `…MissReturnsTypedUnavailable/admitted_server_without_generation`, `…BrokerContactRefusesEachMissingFact/admitted_server_without_generation` |\n179|| R03-broker-decoy-only-admits | narrowing | same site, rev5 R19 shape | KILLED | — | the two `decoy-only_server_admission` subtests |\n180|| R04-unavailable-code-swap-same-exit | narrowing (token) | `backgroundUnavailable` emits `terminal_backend_capability_unproven` (exit 6, registered 1.3.0) with the same typed details (acquire.go:297) | KILLED | — | every miss subtest + Linux miss + `…VerifiesWithoutCreating` ×3: `code = \"terminal_backend_capability_unproven\", want \"capability_unavailable\"` |\n181|| R05-detail-swap-generation | narrowing (detail) | `TmuxServerGeneration` carries `BrokerState` (acquire.go:294) | KILLED | — | every unavailable-asserting test: `detail \"tmux_server_generation\" = absent, want \"generation-7\"` |\n182|| R06-exec-fallback-B9-witness | additive (bound) | direct `os/exec` spawn on the background miss (acquire.go:204) | **SURVIVED** | — | (stated bound B9; observation 1) |\n183|| R07-membership-fresh-decoy-local-attach | narrowing | membership arm admits `local_attach` (readiness.go:40) | **SURVIVED** | KILLED | K07 (P3-B) |\n184|| R08-verify-odirectory-drop-replay | replay | producer `N-containment-odirectory-verify` against the full suite | KILLED | — | `TestVerifyRuntimeDirRefusesNonDirectoryLeaf/{regular_file,fifo_without_blocking}` (5s BLOCK), `TestAcquireBackgroundRefusesNonDirectoryLeaf` |\n185|| R11-background-probe-before-verify | order | broker probed before custody (acquire.go:183-193) | KILLED (8 top-level tests) | — | `…VerifiesWithoutCreating` ×3 (\"broker was probed for an absent runtime directory\"), every background custody test (\"broker was probed past …\") |\n186|| R12-foreground-probe-before-ensure | order | server probed before ensure (acquire.go:228-235) | KILLED | — | `…StagesCommitPhaseCustodyRefusal`, `…RefusesBadRoot/missing` |\n187|| R15-linux-only-fallback-spawn | additive (platform-narrowed) | fallback spawn on a Linux miss (acquire.go:204) | KILLED | — | `TestAcquireBackgroundMissOnLinuxAlsoRefusesWithoutFallback` |\n188|| R16-wsl2-only-fallback-spawn | additive (platform-narrowed) | fallback spawn on a WSL2 miss (acquire.go:204) | **SURVIVED** | KILLED | K16 (P3-A) |\n189|| R17-dispatch-wsl2-background-to-foreground | narrowing | dispatch (acquire.go:163) routes WSL2 background callers foreground | KILLED | — | `…VerifiesWithoutCreating/wsl2` (directory created, spawn 1) |\n190|| R22-collision-skipped-for-background | narrowing (caller axis) | collision gate bypassed for background at the entry (acquire.go:159) | KILLED | — | `TestAcquireRefusesAmbientCollision/*/background` ×5, unclean + TMUX-encoding background legs |\n191|| R23-override-skipped-for-background | narrowing (caller axis) | override gate bypassed for background at the entry (acquire.go:159) | KILLED | — | `TestAcquireRefusesEveryAmbientOverrideVector/*/background` ×6 |\n192|| C-reviewer-control | control | comment-only edit in acquire.go | SURVIVED | — | (must survive; proves the battery observes outcomes) |\n193|| R25-realm-constant-swap-headless | narrowing (token) | `realmCapability` swapped to another registered §4.D value | KILLED | — | every unavailable test (`detail \"capability\"` literal), `…ForegroundRefusesRunningUnattested` (decoy attaches), `…BackgroundContactsBroker` |\n194|| R26-principal-generation-admits-when-server-bound | narrowing | principal-generation arm waived for an attested server (readiness.go:83) | KILLED | — | `generation-unbound_principal` in both tables, `empty_principal_generation`, `both_generations_empty` |\n195|| R27-absence-remap-withheld-on-wsl2 | narrowing | absence remap (acquire.go:184) skipped for WSL2 | KILLED | — | `…VerifiesWithoutCreating/wsl2` |\n196|| R28-effect-census-probe-at-background-top | effect census | guarded `ProbeServer` call at the top of `acquireBackground` | KILLED (16 top-level tests; +1 crash-test flake in run 1 only, observation 2) | — | every background test that enters the function |\n197|\n198|Denominator: 21 applied rows = 12 narrowing + 3 additive + 1 replay + 2 order + 1 effect census\n199|+ 1 control (+ R28 counted once). Of the 12 narrowings, 10 KILLED by the committed suite, 2\n200|SURVIVED (R07 outright; R01 killed only by reroute, admit direction and no-hang unmeasured) —\n201|each proven real by a probe kill (production correct, suite blind). Of the 3 additives, R15 KILLED,\n202|R16 SURVIVED (probe kill), R06 SURVIVED as the stated bound. Replay, both orderings and the effect\n203|census KILLED. Every KILLED row was killed by exactly the tests named above (kill lines in the raw\n204|logs). Passes 1 and 2 identical.\n205|\n206|## §P — reviewer probes (7, `logs/probes-rev6-baseline.log`, all PASS on the untouched candidate)\n207|\n208|K01 `EnsureRuntimeDir` on a 0700 regular-file leaf → `runtime containment` (baseline for R01);\n209|K01b `EnsureRuntimeDir` on a FIFO leaf under a 5s deadline → `runtime containment` immediately;\n210|K01c foreground `Acquire` on the 0700 regular-file leaf → `runtime containment`, no probe, no\n211|spawn; K07 `local_attach`-only admission → `server attestation` at the helper and\n212|`capability_unavailable` through the background miss, spawn 0 (baseline for R07); K16 WSL2\n213|background miss with a present leaf → `capability_unavailable`, spawn 0, probe silent (baseline\n214|for R16); P11 symlinked intermediate root component followed on Ensure and Verify (B11 witness);\n215|P-FIFO FIFO leaf through the background entry → `runtime containment` fast, broker not probed.\n216|\n217|## What held under attack (keep)\n218|\n219|- Dedicated-server rule per vector: override refused on all five members plus whitespace on both\n220|  callers through `Acquire`, and the caller axis of both the override and the collision gate is\n221|  pinned at the entry (R22/R23 KILLED); the socket has exactly one constructor (`SocketPath`,\n222|  called from `ResolveSocket` and `BuildArgv`), one resolution site (`Acquire` → `ResolveSocket`)\n223|  and one spawn site; `Acquire` never reads the environment or execs; the §3.2 path is pinned at\n224|  the entry on both callers and at all three `RuntimeDirName` sites; the argv vector is pinned\n225|  element-by-element at the helper and through the entry.\n226|- Background rules: broker-or-refuse with the literal `capability_unavailable`, exit 6 and the\n227|  five typed details asserted as literals — a same-exit registered code swap (R04), a detail swap\n228|  (R05) and a realm-constant swap (R25) all redden; the broker-side attested-server conjunct is now\n229|  pinned for five admission shapes at the helper AND through the background entry (R02/R03\n230|  KILLED); the principal arms are pinned (R26); the absent-leaf cold state returns the typed\n231|  refusal on macOS, Linux and WSL2 (R27); the fallback is killed through `Spawn`, through\n232|  `acquireForeground` re-entry, on Linux (R15) and at the WSL2 dispatch (R17); custody precedes\n233|  the broker probe (R11) and ensure precedes the server probe (R12). Residue: P3-A.\n234|- Attestation / cached observations: no input exists for a managername hint or a cached sentinel\n235|  (`Request` and `RealmAdmission` have no such member); a replayed observation is a\n236|  stale-generation admission and refuses on both paths; the generation-binding and membership\n237|  arms are pinned at the helper, the broker contact and both entries (the producer's\n238|  `N-realm-membership`/`N-realm-generation` kill through four tables). Residue: P3-B.\n239|- Custody: mode (exact 0700, both sides, both directions), ownership (both sides, and the\n240|  absence classifier's ownership member at the background entry), containment on the verify side\n241|  (FIFO fast-fail, 0700 regular file, symlink leaf, symlink root, handle mismatch) and the\n242|  commit-side symlink leaf/root and mismatch all pinned; the top-level custody oracle sees the\n243|  wrapper; the real-SIGKILL crash test converges. Residue: P2-A (commit-side O_DIRECTORY arm).\n244|- Determinism: 0 SKIP with tmux unresolvable, 190 RUN; no real-tmux witness (B1); no mock-only\n245|  degradation.\n246|- Boundary: `internal/traceability` untouched; README section carries no CLI/capability claim; no\n247|  trunk drift; producer evidence archive complete and digest-verified; LOGBOOK newest-first.\n248|\n249|## Coverage ratio measured against the 58-row table\n250|\n251|**58 of 58 rows are driven as their statements are written**; the ratio is not inflated. The gaps\n252|sit beside the statements, at the member level: row 5 (the commit-side non-directory clause is\n253|driven for a 0600 file, i.e. by the mode gate, and its FIFO clause names one deadline test on one\n254|side — P2-A), rows 29/31 (the miss arm and the no-fallback census cover two of the three tmux\n255|platforms — P3-A), rows 35/27 (one decoy of fourteen — P3-B). Census: 50 of 264 cells measured\n256|as claimed; the `commit × ENS/AFG` cells are the ones whose row lists omit a live arm.\n257|\n258|## Rework scope (for the producer)\n259|\n260|1. **P2-A (tests + row + three sentences, no production change)**: mirror the verify-side\n261|   fixtures on the commit side — 0700 regular-file leaf on `EnsureRuntimeDir` and through\n262|   foreground `Acquire` (assert no probe, no spawn), FIFO leaf on `EnsureRuntimeDir` under\n263|   `verifyWithDeadline` (K01/K01b/K01c in the reviewer probe file are the templates); ship\n264|   `N-containment-odirectory-commit` (drop `O_DIRECTORY` from the commit `Openat`), name it under\n265|   row 5 and in the `commit × ENS` and `commit × AFG` census cells; reword row 5's FIFO clause to\n266|   both deadline tests; fix the `N-containment-odirectory-verify` note.\n267|2. **P3-A**: WSL2 member of the miss table (platform table on the Linux miss test or a WSL2\n268|   subtest), added to `BG_MISS_LINUX` so `N-creation-literal` and both `D-` rows kill on all three\n269|   platforms; name under rows 29/31.\n270|3. **P3-B**: a catalog-derived decoy completeness test (every non-realm `catalog.Current().Capabilities`\n271|   member alone, and all together, refuses at `CheckServerAttested` and through the background\n272|   miss); name under rows 27/35.\n273|4. Optional: capture the crash child's combined output in the failure message; name\n274|   `TestBuildArgvRefusesInvalidArgvShape` under B12; de-duplicate matrix row 46; B12 in the\n275|   `argv × AFG` cell; correct the `N-details-constructor` note.\n276|5. Rerun the package suite (tmux hidden), `GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go vet ./...`, the harness\n277|   twice, and the 30-command suite; refresh results/matrix/archive; hand off as revision 7.\n278|   Everything in \"What held under attack\" needs no change — do not re-litigate it.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
