{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c807","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c5d0-c246-7b92-beac-dc3b11390997"},"sequence":606,"recorded_at":1780531400001207,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"aa3bb7a1-c12a-4660-a0d5-ffba7d41ef0c","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"aa3bb7a1-c12a-4660-a0d5-ffba7d41ef0c","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"aa3bb7a1-c12a-4660-a0d5-ffba7d41ef0c"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c5d2-5bcb-7c61-b099-1a36ff216008"},"task_id":"01a0c5d2-5bcb-7c61-b099-1a36ff216008","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c5d2-5bcb-7c61-b099-1a36ff216008","chunk":"Read text file `internal/tmuxserver/TRACEABILITY.md`.\n1|# TRACEABILITY — internal/tmuxserver (AX v0.7.0)\n2|\n3|Normative scope: AX v0.7.0 Section 3.2 (platform paths: the\n4|dedicated socket `<runtime>/tmux/ax.sock` under the Runtime IPC root;\n5|the socket is runtime IPC, never durable identity), Section 4.2 (tmux\n6|backend: dedicated -S server, no ambient/default discovery or reuse,\n7|credential-sensitive creation, background broker-or-refuse with typed\n8|capability_unavailable and no fallback to direct creation, launchctl\n9|managername as diagnostic hint only, cached observations never\n10|authorize resume), Section 4.C (operation vocabulary cited for the\n11|wrapper entrypoint shape only), Section 4.D (capability evidence cited\n12|landed), and Section 4.E (sensitive runtime state is owner-only and\n13|non-replicable). Story: production-tmux-backend (first leaf).\n14|\n15|Rule: every row names its production entry point. A row is driven only\n16|when the named committed test executes that entry. Prose in place of\n17|the ratio is not evidence. 58 of 58 AC rows driven (row 55 extends\n18|the rows 19-22 override class with the fifth ambient member,\n19|TMUX_TMPDIR; row 56 binds the Section 3.2 path and runtime-root\n20|clause; rows 57-58 pin the commit-failure and whitespace-override\n21|arms); no row is a bound — the stated bounds below cover\n22|deliberately unclaimed surfaces, not undriven rows.\n23|\n24|No test in this package starts a tmux process: every broker, server,\n25|and spawner interaction runs through injected dependencies, and the\n26|suite passes with no tmux installed. No row has a real-tmux witness;\n27|that is the determinism design, not a gap (bound B1).\n28|\n29|Attestation authority: the sentinel/smoke sufficiency, signature\n30|verification, liveness, and expiry verdict is the landed\n31|internal/terminalbackend Reconcile/ResolveEvidence admission,\n32|consumed here as an Admitted set composed only with the generation\n33|equality the wrapper owner (internal/axpane checkRealm) already\n34|enforces. This leaf decides membership plus generation binding and\n35|re-decides nothing the admission proves.\n36|\n37|## Runtime custody (Sections 4.2, 4.E)\n38|\n39|| # | Clause | Call site | Test |\n40||---|--------|-----------|------|\n41|| 1 | Ensure creates the owner-only 0700 directory, explicitly under a restrictive umask | EnsureRuntimeDir (runtime.go, runtime_unix.go) | TestEnsureRuntimeDirCreatesOwnerOnly, TestEnsureRuntimeDirEnforcesModeUnderRestrictiveUmask |\n42|| 2 | Re-ensure is idempotent and verifies mode | EnsureRuntimeDir (runtime.go, runtime_unix.go) | TestEnsureRuntimeDirIsIdempotent |\n43|| 3 | Compliant directory verifies | VerifyRuntimeDir (runtime.go, runtime_unix.go) | TestVerifyRuntimeDirAdmitsCompliant |\n44|| 4 | Widened (0755) and narrower (0600/0500) modes refuse on ensure and verify, never silently repaired | EnsureRuntimeDir, VerifyRuntimeDir (runtime_unix.go) | TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesWidenedMode, TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesNarrowerMode |\n45|| 5 | Non-directory leaf refuses on commit and verify; the verify open carries no O_NONBLOCK by decision — FIFO refusal relies on O_DIRECTORY failing fast, pinned by the deadline test | EnsureRuntimeDir, VerifyRuntimeDir (runtime_unix.go), Acquire (acquire.go, background) | TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesNonDirectoryLeaf, TestVerifyRuntimeDirRefusesNonDirectoryLeaf (regular file, FIFO under deadline), TestAcquireBackgroundRefusesNonDirectoryLeaf, TestAcquireBackgroundRefusesSymlinkLeaf, TestAcquireBackgroundRefusesHandleMismatch |\n46|| 6 | Symlink leaf refuses on commit and verify. On darwin the verify-side ELOOP arm is unreachable — openat(O_NOFOLLOW&#124;O_DIRECTORY) on a symlink leaf returns ENOTDIR — while on Linux the same open returns ELOOP, mapped to containment; reasoned, not run, since the configured suite is darwin-only | EnsureRuntimeDir, VerifyRuntimeDir (runtime_unix.go) | TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesSymlinkLeaf, TestVerifyRuntimeDirRefusesSymlinkLeaf |\n47|| 7 | Foreign ownership refuses on ensure and verify | EnsureRuntimeDir, VerifyRuntimeDir (ownership_unix.go) | TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesForeignOwnership |\n48|| 8 | Handle/path mismatch refuses | EnsureRuntimeDir (runtime.go) | TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesHandleMismatch |\n49|| 9 | Symlinked root refuses on commit, verify, and through the background entry | EnsureRuntimeDir, VerifyRuntimeDir (runtime_unix.go), Acquire (acquire.go, background) | TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesSymlinkRoot, TestVerifyRuntimeDirRefusesSymlinkRoot, TestAcquireBackgroundRefusesSymlinkRoot |\n50|| 10 | Relative, empty, parent, and missing roots refuse invalid (runtime root), the same code verify reports (row 13); the foreground entry refuses a bad root before any side effect | EnsureRuntimeDir (runtime.go, runtime_unix.go), Acquire (acquire.go, foreground) | TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesBadRoots (4 subtests), TestAcquireForegroundRefusesBadRoot (relative, missing) |\n51|| 11 | Empty, dot, parent, nested, absolute, and NUL names refuse | EnsureRuntimeDir (runtime.go) | TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesBadNames (6 subtests) |\n52|| 12 | Unknown platform refuses on commit, verify, and through Acquire on both callers | EnsureRuntimeDir, VerifyRuntimeDir (runtime.go), Acquire (acquire.go) | TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesBadPlatform, TestVerifyRuntimeDirRefusesBadLexical (unknown platform), TestAcquireRefusesUnknownPlatform (foreground, background) |\n53|| 13 | Verify refuses absence (runtime absent) and a missing root (runtime root, aligned with the commit side via the shared classifier) without creating | VerifyRuntimeDir (runtime.go, runtime_unix.go) | TestVerifyRuntimeDirRefusesAbsence, TestVerifyRuntimeDirRefusesBadLexical, TestVerifyRuntimeDirRefusesMissingRoot |\n54|| 14 | Linux and WSL2 share the unix custody discipline | EnsureRuntimeDir (runtime_unix.go) | TestLinuxAndWSL2ShareUnixCustody |\n55|| 15 | Windows platform refuses on every host on commit, verify, and through Acquire on both callers; no tmux directory exists on Windows | EnsureRuntimeDir, VerifyRuntimeDir (runtime.go), Acquire (acquire.go) | TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesWindowsOnUnixHost (commit and verify legs), TestAcquireRefusesWindowsPlatform (foreground, background) |\n56|| 57 | Commit-phase filesystem failure (unwritable root) refuses the commit detail instead of being mistaken for an existing leaf | EnsureRuntimeDir (runtime_unix.go) | TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesReadOnlyRoot |\n57|\n58|## Socket path and runtime root (Section 3.2)\n59|\n60|| # | Clause | Call site | Test |\n61||---|--------|-----------|------|\n62|| 56 | Dedicated socket is `<runtime>/tmux/ax.sock` under the Runtime IPC root (macOS: per-user temporary directory; Linux/WSL2: `$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/ax`), resolved by the landed localstore layout as PathRuntime and supplied by the caller; the socket is runtime IPC, never durable identity. The runtime leaf is not an Acquire input — the entry always passes RuntimeDirName, so the outcome socket is `<Root>/tmux/ax.sock` on both caller paths. The parent's verifiable custody (owned, 0700, component-verified without following a symlink) is rows 1-15; root creation custody is the localstore layout owner's (B19) and provenance is unclaimed (B20) | SocketPath (sock