U2 |\n206|| probe (acquire.go:190,232) | M TestAcquireForegroundProbeFailurePassesThrough / N-probe-swallow-foreground | M TestAcquireBackgroundProbeFailurePassesThrough / N-probe-swallow-background | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 |\n207|| spawn (acquire.go:246) | M TestAcquireForegroundSpawnFailureReportsWithoutFallback + TestAcquireForegroundSpawnIsIdempotentAcrossRetry / N-spawn-swallow | U2 no spawn call on the background path (structural); no-fallback proof is the spy census + D rows at creation × ABG | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 |\n208|| argv (argv.go:17,24) | M TestAcquireForegroundSpawnsDedicatedServer full element compare / N-argv-detached + N-argv-tail (socket/session arms U3: socket always derived, session pre-validated) | U2 background never builds spawn argv | U2 | U2 | M exact-vector + ambient-socket + invalid-shape + malformed-session tests / N-argv-socket + N-argv-tmuxenv + N-argv-shape + N-argv-session + N-argv-detached + N-argv-tail | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 | U2 |\n209|\n210|SOCK (SocketPath) is a pure join and OBS (ObserveAmbient) records\n211|without deciding: neither enforces any gate, so their columns read U\n212|throughout by construction — the wiring gate pins what callers pass\n213|to the join. CRE decides only G-creation; every other CRE cell is U\n214|because the direct entry answers only \"may this caller create\" for\n215|post-gate caller values.\n216|\n217|## Stated bounds\n218|\n219|- B1 Determinism: no row has a real-tmux witness. Every broker, server,\n220|  and spawner interaction runs through injected dependencies; the suite\n221|  passes with no tmux process anywhere. A live-server test would add a\n222|  witness, not a rule, and is sibling scope.\n223|- B2 Windows refusal: native Windows MUST NOT claim tmux (pinned SPEC\n224|  1458). The Windows platform refuses at the lexical gate on every host\n225|  (row 15); the Windows commit/verify arms refuse every platform and\n226|  exist only so the package compiles under GOOS=windows.\n227|- B3 Nil-dependency weakening on the foreground path panics instead of\n228|  misbehaving; the narrowing row pins the refusal and discloses the\n229|  panic kill.\n230|- B4 No gate inspects source text, so no token-preserving mutant\n231|  applies; the harness executes the behavioral suite.\n232|- B5 Attach presentation vectors are sibling scope: attached and broker\n233|  outcomes carry the socket, and only the spawned outcome carries argv.\n234|- B6 Lifecycle operations (create, attach, status, quiesce, stop,\n235|  terminate, restore) belong to the sibling leaves, not to acquisition.\n236|- B7 The handle-mismatch arm stages its race through the sameDirectory\n237|  seam; a true concurrent handle swap is not staged.\n238|- B8 Registry bindings and the digest re-pin belong to the story's\n239|  final leaf; this leaf documents clause coverage here and in the\n240|  conformance matrix only.\n241|- B9 Adapter split: this leaf ships the decision core and argv only. No\n242|  production probe or spawner implementation exists in the tree; the\n243|  exec/probe adapters that report Reconcile/ResolveEvidence verdicts\n244|  and spawn through the built argv, and the server socket's crash\n245|  evidence, are owned by the lifecycle leaf TASK-260830-1c28dz. The\n246|  no-fallback proof covers spawns routed through Dependencies.Spawn;\n247|  a fallback through a direct os/exec call is excluded today only by\n248|  the import census (no os/exec import in the package).\n249|  Dependencies.Spawn is inert on the background path: a nil spawner\n250|  with a live broker still contacts (the broker path never calls it),\n251|  so the field is dead weight there — which is what makes the\n252|  shared-Dependencies fallback shape realistic, and why the spy\n253|  census arms the foreground probe alongside the spawner.\n254|- B10 Crash convergence assumes a umask that preserves owner rwx\n255|  (umask & 0700 == 0). Under an owner-bit-stripping umask a leaf\n256|  stranded between mkdirat and the explicit chmod refuses on retry\n257|  instead of converging, because existing leaves verify, never repair.\n258|- B11 A symlinked intermediate component inside the root path is\n259|  followed; only the root's last component refuses (row 9). This\n260|  matches the landed secprim root open and is the same bound.\n261|- B12 The landed argv shape refusal (BuildArgv via secprim.CheckArgv)\n262|  is reachable only by direct call with a non-filesystem runtime dir;\n263|  through Acquire the directory always names a created directory.\n264|- B13 Sentinel/smoke sufficiency, signature verification, liveness,\n265|  and expiry are the landed Reconcile admission's verdict, consumed\n266|  here through Has. This leaf decides membership plus generation\n267|  binding only; the host-binding and provider-build cross-bind the\n268|  wrapper evaluates stays with the lifecycle owner.\n269|- B14 The battery and the read-only-root test assume a non-root test\n270|  user: N-fchmod-umask admits non-root creates past the explicit\n271|  chmod, so under root it is equivalent to the original and survives,\n272|  and TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesReadOnlyRoot stages a genuine EACCES\n273|  only when permission bits bind the test user. The reviewer's\n274|  same-shaped plant carries the identical assumption.\n275|- B15 Unmeasured fail-closed stat arms, no seam: handleBoundToPath's\n276|  two stat-failure arms (runtime.go) and verifyOwnership's !ok arm\n277|  (ownership_unix.go) fail closed by code and are prose only by test —\n278|  no test can stage a Stat failure on an open directory handle, or a\n279|  stat without ownership metadata on unix, without a seam. The\n280|  guard.Resolve refusal arm (runtime.go) is unreachable through the\n281|  name grammar: every input the guard would refuse is refused earlier\n282|  by scalar, so the fail-open plant survives by construction. The\n283|  secprim.NewGuard refusal arm (runtime.go:94-96) is the same class:\n284|  no committed input reaches it. The same unstageable class covers\n285|  the commit-side Fchmod and parent-Fsync failure arms and the\n286|  commit-side (runtime_unix.go:76-79) and verify-side leaf-Stat\n287|  failure arms: no committed test stages those failures. An\n288|  unopenable (0000) root reports `runtime containment` on both entries\n289|  with no committed test staging it — classifying EACCES as missing\n290|  would reroute it to `runtime root`, refusal-to-refusal. Reported\n291|  as error-arm rows, never counted among the narrowing survivors.\n292|- B16 The collision gate compares cleaned byte strings: an ambient\n293|  value naming the derived socket through a symlinked or relative\n294|  alias of the root walks past it (realpath equivalence is not\n295|  applied, and a cwd-relative spelling never equals the absolute\n296|  derived socket). Roots containing a comma are outside the TMUX\n297|  member's encoding: the gate splits at the first comma exactly as\n298|  tmux(1) itself does, so a comma-root socket component walks past\n299|  it. The spec rule is unaffected — the socket is derived, never\n300|  selected from an ambient value — so this bounds only the\n301|  package-local defense-in-depth claim. An `ax` invocation from\n302|  inside its own AX pane refuses `ambient collision` when the caller\n303|  populates Ambient from the process environment\n304|  (TMUX=`<derived>`,pid,idx in the real encoding): over-strict\n305|  rather than over-permissive, and the caller owns what it observes\n306|  — the lifecycle leaf TASK-260830-1c28dz decides the\n307|  nested-invocation rule deliberately.\n308|- B17 The mode gate reads permission bits only: setgid/sticky bits on\n309|  a 0700 leaf are admitted and macOS ACLs are not inspected. This\n310|  matches the landed hosttrust custody precedent\n311|  (internal/hosttrust/custody_unix.go platformModeOK: Perm() == mode),\n312|  so it is the same bound, not a fork.\n313|- B18 The derived socket path is not checked against the platform\n314|  sun_path limit (104 bytes on macOS); a deep runtime root surfaces\n315|  as a spawn failure in the lifecycle leaf's adapter, owned by\n316|  TASK-260830-1c28dz.\n317|- B19 The Runtime IPC root's own mode and ownership are not gated in\n318|  this leaf: the root arrives as the caller-supplied\n319|  localstore-resolved PathRuntime value, its creation-time custody is\n320|  the localstore layout owner's, and the SPEC 810-812\n321|  before-bind/connect rejection of an unsafe path, parent, or ancestor\n322|  is the lifecycle bind step's (TASK-260830-1c28dz), which is the step\n323|  that binds. This leaf pins the root handle (no-follow open plus\n324|  handle/path binding) and commits the leaf relative to it; a\n325|  world-writable root is admitted here and refused at bind. That the\n326|  root value is the landed localstore PathRuntime is a contract\n327|  statement about the caller, not a driven fact: no test composes\n328|  localstore with Acquire.\n329|- B20 Whether the runtime leaf was created by AX is indistinguishable\n330|  after the fact: any same-user 0700 directory under an admitted name\n331|  is accepted. The verifiable properties — mode, ownership, kind,\n332|  containment — are gated (rows 1-15); provenance is not claimed.\n333|- B21 No broker is modelled as the zero BrokerReport, whose\n334|  Principal.UID is 0: for a non-root process the absent broker\n335|  refuses on the authentication arm, while under a root process the\n336|  same-user arm passes and refusal comes from the generation arm.\n337|  The broker-path outcome socket binding is the generation equality\n338|  only — BrokerReport carries no socket of its own.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
