{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000ca47","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c5d0-c246-7b92-beac-dc3b11390997"},"sequence":894,"recorded_at":1780531400001783,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"aa3bb7a1-c12a-4660-a0d5-ffba7d41ef0c","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"aa3bb7a1-c12a-4660-a0d5-ffba7d41ef0c","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"aa3bb7a1-c12a-4660-a0d5-ffba7d41ef0c"},"call_id":"call_01a0c5d388d0769daa839e570517dcc8","text":"Read text file `internal/tmuxserver/acquire_test.go`.\n(214 line(s) above)\n215|func TestAcquireForegroundRefusesMalformedSession(t *testing.T) {\n216|\troot := runtimeRoot(t)\n217|\treq := validRequest(t, root)\n218|\treq.SessionID = \"12345\"\n219|\tspy := &spawnSpy{}\n220|\tprobed := false\n221|\treq.Deps.ProbeServer = func(socket string) (ServerReport, error) {\n222|\t\tprobed = true\n223|\t\treturn ServerReport{}, nil\n224|\t}\n225|\treq.Deps.Spawn = spy.spawn\n226|\t_, err := Acquire(req)\n227|\trequireLocalError(t, err, \"tmux_invalid_arguments\", \"session identity\")\n228|\tif probed {\n229|\t\tt.Fatal(\"server was probed before a malformed session refused\")\n230|\t}\n231|\tif spy.calls != 0 {\n232|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"spawn calls = %d, want 0\", spy.calls)\n233|\t}\n234|\tif _, statErr := os.Lstat(filepath.Join(root, RuntimeDirName)); !os.IsNotExist(statErr) {\n235|\t\tt.Fatalf(\"malformed session created the directory: stat err = %v\", statErr)\n236|\t}\n237|}\n238|\n239|// A malformed runtime root refuses through the foreground entry with\n240|// no directory, no probe, and no spawn: the lexical gate precedes\n241|// every side effect on the creating path too.\n242|func TestAcquireForegroundRefusesBadRoot(t *testing.T) {\n243|\troot := runtimeRoot(t)\n244|\tfor _, tc := range []struct {\n245|\t\tname string\n246|\t\troot string\n247|\t}{\n248|\t\t{\"relative\", \"relative/root\"},\n249|\t\t{\"missing\", filepath.Join(root, \"no-such-root\")},\n250|\t} {\n251|\t\tt.Run(tc.name, func(t *testing.T) {\n252|\t\t\tleaf := filepath.Join(root, RuntimeDirName)\n253|\t\t\treq := validRequest(t, tc.root)\n254|\t\t\tspy := &spawnSpy{}\n255|\t\t\tprobed := false\n256|\t\t\treq.Deps.ProbeServer = func(socket string) (ServerReport, error) {\n257|\t\t\t\tprobed = true\n258|\t\t\t\treturn ServerReport{}, nil\n259|\t\t\t}\n260|\t\t\treq.Deps.Spawn = spy.spawn\n261|\t\t\t_, err := Acquire(req)\n262|\t\t\trequireLocalError(t, err, \"tmux_invalid_arguments\", \"runtime root\")\n263|\t\t\tif probed {\n264|\t\t\t\tt.Fatal(\"server was probed before a bad root refused\")\n265|\t\t\t}\n266|\t\t\tif spy.calls != 0 {\n267|\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"spawn calls = %d, want 0\", spy.calls)\n268|\t\t\t}\n269|\t\t\tif _, statErr := os.Lstat(leaf); !os.IsNotExist(statErr) {\n270|\t\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"bad root created the directory: stat err = %v\", statErr)\n271|\t\t\t}\n272|\t\t})\n273|\t}\n274|}\n275|\n276|func TestAcquireBackgroundContactsBroker(t *testing.T) {\n277|\troot := runtimeRoot(t)\n278|\truntimeDir(t, root)\n279|\treq := validRequest(t, root)\n280|\treq.Caller = CallerBackground\n281|\treq.Platform = scalar.PlatformMacOS\n282|\tspy := &spawnSpy{}\n283|\tprobe := &probeServerSpy{}\n284|\tprobed := false\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000ca49","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c5d0-c246-7b92-beac-dc3b11390997"},"sequence":895,"recorded_at":1780531400001785,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"aa3bb7a1-c12a-4660-a0d5-ffba7d41ef0c","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"aa3bb7a1-c12a-4660-a0d5-ffba7d41ef0c","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"aa3bb7a1-c12a-4660-a0d5-ffba7d41ef0c"},"call_id":"call_01a0c5d38b997243a6696bba8d111427","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-35urbp/TASK-260830-35urbp_results.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-35urbp results — implement-private-tmux-server-management (rev6)\n2|\n3|Rework of revision 5 after review-verdict-rev5 (CHANGES REQUESTED: no\n4|P1, one P2 class with four measured members, two P3). First leaf of\n5|STORY-260830-2t4g7i (production-tmux-backend, EPIC M1). The reviewer\n6|states every rev4 finding is closed with driven evidence and stays\n7|closed, and that production behaves correctly at every point the\n8|review drove; this revision keeps all of that and changes only what\n9|the verdict grades open, plus what the gate × entry census surfaced.\n10|\n11|Candidate: UNCOMMITTED working tree on branch\n12|`task-board/story/STORY-260830-2t4g7i` atop trunk `799c338` (trunk\n13|unmoved since rev5; no refresh, no rebase, no commit, no merge by this\n14|run). `git status` shows only `internal/tmuxserver/`, `README.md`,\n15|`LOGBOOK.md`.\n16|\n17|Normative source: the pinned `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md`\n18|§3.2 platform paths (lines 765-813: the dedicated socket\n19|`<runtime>/tmux/ax.sock` under the Runtime IPC root) and §4.2 tmux\n20|backend (lines 1403-1449), with §4.C (1082), §4.D (1220), and\n21|§4.E (1309) as context, plus §4.3 (1458) and §4.4 for the Windows\n22|and broker rules. All clause citations name the pinned file, never\n23|the network, never v0.5.0.\n24|\n25|## Finding-by-finding table (verdict -> change -> test that fails without it -> evidence)\n26|\n27|| Finding | Change | Test that fails without it | Evidence path |\n28||---|---|---|---|\n29|| P2-A broker-or-refuse pinned at the entry only for fixture shapes: zero admission (R09), admitted-without-generation (R10), decoy-only (R19) server shapes walk through; ProbeServer unarmed on every background test (R18 fallback guard invisible) | Three server-admission subtests added to `TestAcquireBackgroundMissReturnsTypedUnavailable` AND mirrored in `TestCheckBrokerContactRefusesEachMissingFact`; shipped `N-broker-zero-admission` at the `CheckBrokerContact` server wiring (R09 shape; R10/R19 share the anchor); fail-if-called `ProbeServer` spy armed in every background-path `Acquire` test (23/23 mechanical census); shipped `D-background-fallback-foreground` (R18 shape); row-31/README sentence extended to both foreground dependencies | The three new miss-table subtests + the three broker-contact mirror subtests (R09/R10/R19 shapes redden both tables firsthand); every miss-table subtest reddens under D-background-fallback-foreground | `harness-pass1/N-broker-zero-admission.log`, `harness-pass1/D-background-fallback-foreground.log` (+ pass 2), `logs/R10-R19-anchor-share.log` (unshipped-shape replay: both shapes KILLED by the new tests through both tables) |\n30|| P3-A absence classifier pinned at the entry for mode and containment only (ownership member walks through, R01) | New `TestAcquireBackgroundStagesOwnershipRefusal` (unix-only file, `effectiveUID` seam) asserting top-level `tmux_unsafe_runtime_dir at runtime ownership` with no broker contact and both spies silent; shipped `N-absence-remap-ownership` (R01 shape); sibling rows `N-absence-remap-containment` (R02) and `N-absence-remap-invalid` so every classifier member carries a row | `TestAcquireBackgroundStagesOwnershipRefusal` (foreign-owned leaf maps to `capability_unavailable` under the mutant; the top-level assertion reddens) | `harness-pass1/N-absence-remap-ownership.log`, `N-absence-remap-containment.log`, `N-absence-remap-invalid.log` (+ pass 2) |\n31|| P3-B censusable \"before\" that is false (malformed session creates the directory and probes before refusing, P01) | Session identity parses at the foreground entry before `EnsureRuntimeDir` and the probe; no-directory/no-probe assertions added to `TestAcquireForegroundRefusesMalformedSession`; shipped `N-session-entry` | `TestAcquireForegroundRefusesMalformedSession` (under the mutant the request creates the directory and probes before the spawn-site refusal, tripping the new assertions while the refusal code stays correct) | `harness-pass1/N-session-entry.log` (+ pass 2), `logs/pkg-tests-v.log` |\n32|| Obs-1 comma root walks past the TMUX split (P02) | Row 23/B16 scope comma roots out of the TMUX member's encoding (faithful to tmux(1) itself) | — (bound/prose, no behavior) | `TRACEABILITY.md` rows 23/B16 |\n33|| Obs-2 relative alias walks past the cleaned-string gate (P03) | B16 reads \"symlinked or relative alias\" | — (bound/prose, no behavior) | `TRACEABILITY.md` B16 |\n34|| Obs-3 Spawn inert on the background path (P04) | B9 + row 31 state the inert field and why the shared-Dependencies fallback shape is realistic | — (design note; the D-background-fallback-foreground row measures the fallback) | `TRACEABILITY.md` B9, row 31 |\n35|| Obs-5 input-reachable constructor-failure arm unpinned (P06) | New `TestAcquireBackgroundInvalidGenerationRefusesAfterProbe` (invalid-UTF-8 generation refuses after the broker probe) + shipped `N-details-constructor`; B15 names the commit-side leaf-`Stat` and `NewGuard` arms | The new test (under the mutant the miss reports a zero outcome with nil error) | `harness-pass1/N-details-constructor.log` (+ pass 2) |\n36|| Obs-6 static-gate exits live in prose only | `static-gates.log` records every exit code | — (evidence hygiene) | `logs/static-gates.log` |\n37|\n38|Kept untouched per the verdict: the dedicated-server rule per vector,\n39|the background broker-or-refuse wiring with the literal\n40|`capability_unavailable` and typed details, the no-fallback rule along\n41|the caller/credential/platform axes, the landed-admission attestation\n42|composition, the custody gates that held under attack (FIFO/symlink/\n43|mode/UID/handle-mismatch refusals, the explicit `Fchmod`, the\n44|real-SIGKILL crash test), the determinism design (no real-tmux\n45|witness), and the `internal/traceability` boundary.\n46|\n47|## The instrument: gate × entry census (the rework brief's deliverable)\n48|\n49|Three rounds in a row produced the same finding class at a new site\n50|each time (rev3 P2-C foreground admission data, rev4 P2-B\n51|Request.Name, rev5 P2-A broker-server wiring): the defect was the\n52|measurement, not the code. This revision ships the instrument: for\n53|every gate in the package, every production entry that can reach it —\n54|`Acquire` foreground, `Acquire` background, `EnsureRuntimeDir`,\n55|`VerifyRuntimeDir`, `BuildArgv`, `SocketPath`, `ResolveSocket`,\n56|`ObserveAmbient`, `CheckBrokerContact`, `CheckServerAttested`, and\n57|`checkCreationAllowed` called directly — with exactly one of: a\n58|named committed test driving the gate through that entry plus an\n59|admitting narrowing row killing through that test; `unreachable` with\n60|the structural reason; or a stated bound. The census is a table in\n61|the conformance matrix, mirrored in TRACEABILITY.md.\n62|\n63|Measured ratio: 50 of 264 cells measured (M), 4 bounds (B, all in the\n64|guard gate's unreachable arm), 210 unreachable with reasons (U); every\n65|reachable non-bound cell is measured (50 of 54). Cell counts verified\n66|mechanically from the table source; every named test exists in the\n67|committed suite and every named row exists in the harness (verified by\n68|script, no dangling references). Multi-entry rows list every entry\n69|their killers cover, with per-entry kill attribution verified from\n70|the raw logs (e.g. N-realm-membership fails all four tables;\n71|N-wiring-ensure fails the foreground leg only, N-wiring-verify the\n72|background leg only).\n73|\n74|Building the census surfaced member gaps beyond the four the reviewer\n75|measured, all closed in this revision: caller-dimension subtests on\n76|the pre-dispatch gates (override/collision/details/unknown-platform\n77|tables drive both callers); N-dispatch-foreground/N-dispatch-background\n78|for the caller→path routing; N-wiring-lexical/ensure/verify for the\n79|three RuntimeDirName sites; N-details-generation/brokerstate (the\n80|reviewer's R11/R12 shapes); N-root-symlink-commit/verify plus\n81|verify- and background-entry symlink-root tests; N-argv-detached/tail\n82|with a full element-by-element vector assertion through the spawn\n83|entry; background-entry symlink-leaf and handle-mismatch tests; run-mask\n84|extensions so shared-site rows kill through every entry they cover.\n85|\n86|## Deliverable (rev6 shape)\n87|\n88|`internal/tmuxserver`, composing the landed owners (never forked):\n89|\n90|- (1) Runtime custody: `EnsureRuntimeDir` / `VerifyRuntimeDir` with\n91|  three independent gates (containment, exact `0700`, eUID ownership).\n92|  Foreground acquisition ensures idempotently; background acquisition\n93|  verifies the existing directory and never creates it. Absence\n94|  (`ENOENT`) carries its own detail; the missing-root mapping is one\n95|  shared classifier; every classifier member (mode, ownership,\n96|  containment, invalid) carries an entry-level test plus a narrowing\n97|  row.\n98|- (2) Dedicated socket: `SocketPath` / `ResolveSocket` derive\n99|  `<root>/tmux/ax.sock` — the spec's path — and refuse overrides and\n100|  ambient collisions on all five members plus whitespace, on both\n101|  callers and at `ResolveSocket` directly, with the TMUX member\n102|  compared in its real encoding and unclean spellings cleaned\n103|  (symlinked, relative, and comma-root aliases bound). The runtime\n104|  leaf is not an `Acquire` input: the entry always passes\n105|  `RuntimeDirName`, pinned at all three sites by narrowings.\n106|- (3) Acquisition: `Acquire` dispatches by caller (routing pinned by\n107|  narrowings both directions), refuses malformed input (including the\n108|  session identity), ambient reuse, and missing dependencies before\n109|  any side effect on both paths. Foreground attaches or spawns (a\n110|  running server never spawns, even with empty admission; the spawn\n111|  vector is pinned element-by-element through the entry);\n112|  background brokers-or-refuses with the typed\n113|  `capability_unavailable` — including the absent-leaf cold state on\n114|  macOS, Linux, and WSL2 — and no fallback (the miss path consults\n115|  the creation gate by call; every background-path `Acquire` test\n116|  arms both a spy spawner and a spy server probe).\n117|- (4) Readiness: `CheckServerAttested` / `CheckBrokerContact` decide\n118|  the landed admission (`Admitted.Has(realm)` + generation equality)\n119|  over a typed same-user generation-bound broker principal. The\n120|  broker-side server wiring is pinned for five admission shapes\n121|  (unattested, stale, zero, admitted-without-generation, decoy-only)\n122|  at the helper and through the background entry. A stale\n123|  admission — the replayed-cached shape — refuses on both paths.\n124|- (5) Spawn argv: `BuildArgv` emits exactly\n125|  `tmux -S socket new-session -d -s session ax pane session`\n126|  through the landed argv gate. Native Windows refuses every request.\n127|\n128|Extended vs deliberately not extended (unchanged from rev5; the\n129|reviewer verified each claim rather than accepting it):\n130|\n131|- Extended (composed): `terminalbackend.Admitted` (attestation\n132|  verdict), `axpane` caller vocabulary, `axerror` typed refusal,\n133|  `scalar` platform/path/UUIDv7 grammars, `secprim` Guard /\n134|  `OpenNoFollowDir` / `CheckArgv`, the `localstore` Runtime IPC root\n135|  (`PathRuntime`, consumed as the caller-supplied `Request.Root` —\n136|  this leaf resolves no root of its own), the `hosttrust`\n137|  verify-never-repair precedent, the `termbind` crash-hook pattern.\n138|- Deliberately not extended: `hosttrust` custody itself (Host Channel\n139|  authority — a tmux runtime dir is not a trust store);\n140|  `terminalbackend` Reconcile evidence admission (consumed, not\n141|  re-owned); `axpane` checkRealm (unexported; this leaf composes the\n142|  same Has-plus-generation-equality over the probe-reported verdict);\n143|  the host-binding/provider-build cross-bind (stays with the lifecycle\n144|  owner, bound B13); `terminstance` lifecycle execution (sibling leaf);\n145|  `secprim`'s private `guardRootMatches` (mirrored as\n146|  `handleBoundToPath` with a seam because the original is unexported);\n147|  `internal/traceability` (untouched — bindings and the re-pin belong\n148|  to the final leaf).\n149|\n150|Determinism: every broker, server, and spawner interaction runs\n151|through injected dependencies. No test starts a tmux process; the\n152|suite passes with the tmux binary unresolvable, `TMUX`/`TMUX_TMPDIR`\n153|unset, and no tmux process on the host (190 PASS — 79 top-level, 111\n154|nested — 0 SKIP in the tmux-hidden run, with the env proof in the\n155|log). No AC row\n156|has a real-tmux witness — that is the design, not a gap (bound B1).\n157|\n158|## Coverage ratio (measured, not planned)\n159|\n160|**58 of 58 AC rows driven** through production entries by named\n161|committed tests — matrix in `internal/tmuxserver/TRACEABILITY.md`,\n162|reproduced with spec-clause mapping in\n163|`TASK-260830-35urbp_conformance-matrix.md` (rev6). Rows 27/28/35/36\n164|name the five-shape server pins at the helper and both entries, row 31\n165|names the 23-test both-spy census and both D rows, row 52 names the\n166|mode/ownership/containment pins, row 45 names the entry session check\n167|with its side-effect assertions, row 23/B16 carry the comma/alias\n168|bounds, row 50 names the invalid-detail arm, and the mutant-to-gate\n169|map names all 72 narrowing rows. The gate × entry census (50 of 264\n170|cells measured, 4 bounds, 210 unreachable with reasons) is the\n171|matrix's own table, mirrored in TRACEABILITY.md.\n172|\n173|## Mutants (shipped harness, per-plant raw logs)\n174|\n175|`PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/tmuxserver/mutant_harness.py` —\n176|72 narrowing + 2 supplementary additive (D-background-fallback,\n177|D-background-fallback-foreground, labeled) + 1 harmless SURVIVED\n178|control. Pass 1 and pass 2: **75/75 each, verdict lists identical**,\n179|exit 0. Per-row raw logs (go output + subprocess exit) for both passes\n180|are in the evidence tarball; production blobs byte-identical\n181|before/after every run (`git status` shows only candidate paths). No\n182|token-preserving source-text mutant applies: no gate inspects source\n183|text (stated bound B4, harness executes the behavioral suite). The one\n184|nil-dependency narrowing that kills by panic (N-deps-foreground) is\n185|disclosed in the harness and the matrix; N-deps-background kills by\n186|an unavailable-vs-dependencies mismatch since the admitted request\n187|reaches Verify on the absent leaf. N-fchmod-umask and the\n188|read-only-root test assume a non-root test user (bound B14), the same\n189|shape as the reviewer's plant. N-broker-empty-generation,\n190|N-commit-eacces-as-exist, and the background leg of\n191|N-verify-absence-detail kill by reroute to a neighboring refusal,\n192|disclosed in their row notes. N-details-constructor kills by nil\n193|success (the swallowed constructor failure reports a zero outcome\n194|with no error). N-session-entry kills through the side-effect\n195|assertions while the refusal code stays correct. The reviewers'\n196|error-arm plants (stat-failure arms flipped to fail-open, the\n197|unreachable guard arm, the unopenable-root arm) are reported as\n198|error-arm rows under bound B15 and are never counted among the\n199|narrowing survivors.\n200|\n201|## Crash / idempotency (unchanged from rev5)\n202|\n203|Real SIGKILL seam (unix): `TestEnsureCrashChildSelfTerminates`\n204|(child runs the genuine `EnsureRuntimeDir` entry and kills itself in\n205|`AfterMkdir`, after mkdirat and before verification plus parent\n206|fsync; parent proves the retry converges to the one verified\n207|directory). Idempotent replay: `TestEnsureRuntimeDirIsIdempotent`,\n208|`TestAcquireCreatesRuntimeDirIdempotently`,\n209|`TestAcquireForegroundSpawnIsIdempotentAcrossRetry` (spawn-then-retry\n210|attaches with exactly one spawn). Crash convergence states the umask\n211|bound B10; the server socket's crash evidence is owned by the\n212|lifecycle leaf (bound B9).\n213|\n214|## Validation (all run firsthand in this session)\n215|\n216|Configured suite read from `spawn.worktree_isolation.validation.commands`\n217|(count 30, verified by read). All 30 green, run by this run (nothing\n218|accepted from rev5 or from construction):\n219|\n220|- 1 gofmt clean (empty file list); 2 `go build ./...` exit 0;\n221|  3 `go vet ./...` exit 0.\n222|- 4 `go test ./... -count=1` exit 0: 45/45 packages ok, 0 package\n223|  FAIL.\n224|- 5 race gate exit 0 with no DATA RACE: run in 6 bounded groups\n225|  (8/8/8/8/8/5 packages = all 45 from `go list ./...`) because one\n226|  shell call is time-bounded; same flags otherwise\n227|  (`-race -count=1 -timeout 25m`). 45/45 ok.\n228|- 6 `go test ./... -cover -count=1` exit 0: 45/45 ok.\n229|  `go test ./internal/tmuxserver/ -cover` 92.7% statements.\n230|- 7-23 all 17 fuzz seeds exit 0. 24 tracecheck exit 0 (70/574).\n231|  25 cataloggen -check exit 0. 26 linux build exit 0. 27 windows build\n232|  exit 0. 28 JSON parse exit 0. 29 `task-board validate` exit 0 (with\n233|  the board's pre-existing 180 issues). 30 `git diff --check` exit 0.\n234|- Repository gates beyond the 30: `GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go vet\n235|  ./...` exit 0, `GOOS=windows go test -c ./internal/tmuxserver`\n236|  exit 0, `GOOS=linux go vet ./internal/tmuxserver` exit 0 (+\n237|  test-compile), `go vet ./internal/tmuxserver` exit 0, gofmt empty;\n238|  package suite 190 RUN / 190 PASS (79 top-level) / 0 SKIP;\n239|  tmux-hidden suite (tmux unresolvable, `TMUX`/`TMUX_TMPDIR` unset, no\n240|  tmux process) exit 0 with 190 PASS and 0 SKIP.\n241|\n242|Reran myself: everything above, plus the mutant battery (targeted\n243|subsets during development + two full logged passes) and the\n244|R10/R19 anchor-share replay. Accepted from already-attached evidence:\n245|nothing — rev5 evidence is superseded by this revision.\n246|\n247|`internal/traceability` untouched; README section updated (72-row\n248|battery count, both-spy census sentence) with exact test commands and\n249|no CLI/capability claim; LOGBOOK rev6 entry added newest-first. The\n250|candidate is UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree.\n251|\n252|## Rejection-pattern self-check\n253|\n254|(a) Literals asserted from spec text at entries (`capability_unavailable`\n255|plus all five typed details, exit 6; `\"tmux\"`/`\"ax.sock\"` plus the\n256|joined `<root>/tmux/ax.sock` at `SocketPath` AND through `Acquire` on\n257|both callers; `ax`/`pane`/UUID session tail; the full spawn vector\n258|element-by-element at `BuildArgv` AND through `Acquire`; `0700`\n259|on both the widened and narrower sides; caller vocabulary;\n260|`credential_capable_execution_realm` as the admitted member, including\n261|the both-empty pair), never production constants. (b) Every rule driven\n262|through the entry the matrix names — and now every (gate, entry) cell\n263|names its own test plus row in the census; the creation gate is\n264|enforced by a call on the background miss path, custody refusals are\n265|staged through `Acquire` on both paths on every member (including the\n266|verify-side symlink leaf/root and handle mismatch on the background\n267|entry, and the absence/missing-root split on three platforms), the\n268|Running arm is pinned at the entry for admission-empty servers, the\n269|spec path is pinned at the entry on both callers with per-site\n270|narrowings, the dispatch is pinned both directions, and the collision\n271|normalization plus TMUX encoding are driven at both\n272|`ResolveSocket` and `Acquire` on both callers. (c) Landed owners composed\n273|(listed above, now including the `localstore` runtime root) — only\n274|package-specific rules are new; the rev1 fork stays deleted. (d) Inputs\n275|driven, effects asserted (spy call counts on both dependencies, argv\n276|bytes, socket equality, typed details, attach vs refuse on stale vs\n277|bound vs empty vs decoy admissions, deadline-bounded FIFO refusal);\n278|the census maps measurement, it substitutes for none — every M cell\n279|carries a test that fails without the property. (e) 72 narrowing rows\n280|+ 2 labeled additives + applied SURVIVED control, one raw log per\n281|plant per run, narrowing-vs-additive stated per row; per-entry kill\n282|attribution verified from the raw logs; error-arm rows reported\n283|separately, never counted as narrowings. (f) Every \"never/composes\"\n284|sentence is backed by a failing-without test or stated as an explicit\n285|bound (B1-B21); the universal spy sentence is a mechanical 23/23\n286|census, and the \"before any side effect\" sentence is pinned by\n287|no-directory/no-probe assertions plus N-session-entry.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
