{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000caa1","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c5d0-c246-7b92-beac-dc3b11390997"},"sequence":939,"recorded_at":1780531400001873,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"aa3bb7a1-c12a-4660-a0d5-ffba7d41ef0c","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"aa3bb7a1-c12a-4660-a0d5-ffba7d41ef0c","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"aa3bb7a1-c12a-4660-a0d5-ffba7d41ef0c"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c5d3-b4b2-79e2-a4a8-75204e22668f"},"task_id":"01a0c5d3-b4b2-79e2-a4a8-75204e22668f","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c5d3-b4b2-79e2-a4a8-75204e22668f","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-35urbp/TASK-260830-35urbp_conformance-matrix.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-35urbp conformance matrix — implement-private-tmux-server-management (rev6)\n2|\n3|Authority: pinned `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md`. Every row names the\n4|spec clause in the spec's own words, the production call site, and the\n5|named committed test that drives it through that entry. 58 of 58 rows\n6|driven (row 55 extends the rows 19-22 override class with the fifth\n7|ambient member; row 56 binds the Section 3.2 path and runtime-root\n8|clause; rows 57-58 pin the commit-failure and whitespace-override\n9|arms). Bounds B1-B21 are stated in\n10|`internal/tmuxserver/TRACEABILITY.md`. Changes from rev5: rows\n11|27/28/35/36 name the five-shape server pins at the helper and both\n12|entries plus the broker-wiring narrowing; row 31 names the 23-test\n13|both-spy census and the second D row; row 52 names the\n14|mode/ownership/containment pins; row 45 names the entry session check\n15|with its side-effect assertions; rows 9/10/12/15 name the new\n16|verify- and Acquire-level lexical pins; row 23/B16 carry the\n17|comma/alias bounds; row 50 names the invalid-detail arm; the mutant\n18|map carries 17 new narrowing rows plus the second additive row; and\n19|the gate × entry census below is new.\n20|\n21|Attestation authority: sentinel/smoke sufficiency, signature\n22|verification, liveness, and expiry are the landed\n23|`internal/terminalbackend` Reconcile/ResolveEvidence admission verdict,\n24|consumed here as an `Admitted` set composed only with the generation\n25|equality `internal/axpane` checkRealm enforces. This leaf decides\n26|membership plus generation binding and re-decides nothing.\n27|\n28|## §3.2 socket path and runtime root\n29|\n30|| # | Clause (spec words) | Call site | Test |\n31||---|---------------------|-----------|------|\n32|| 56 | Dedicated socket is `<runtime>/tmux/ax.sock` under the Runtime IPC root (macOS: per-user temporary directory; Linux/WSL2: `$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/ax`), resolved by the landed localstore layout as PathRuntime and supplied by the caller; the socket is runtime IPC, never durable identity. The runtime leaf is not an Acquire input: the entry always passes RuntimeDirName, so the outcome socket is `<Root>/tmux/ax.sock` on both caller paths | `SocketPath` (socket.go), `Acquire` (acquire.go) | TestSocketPathDerivesOnlyFromRuntimeDir, TestAcquireOutcomeSocketEqualsSpecPath (foreground, background) |\n33|\n34|## §4.2 dedicated -S server; no ambient/default discovery or reuse\n35|\n36|| # | Clause (spec words) | Call site | Test |\n37||---|---------------------|-----------|------|\n38|| 16 | AX MUST use its dedicated `-S` server, as `<root>/tmux/ax.sock` with both leaves asserted as spec literals; the Acquire outcome socket equals `<Root>/tmux/ax.sock` on both caller paths | `SocketPath` (socket.go), `Acquire` (acquire.go) | TestSocketPathDerivesOnlyFromRuntimeDir, TestAcquireOutcomeSocketEqualsSpecPath (foreground, background) |\n39|| 17 | MUST NOT discover or reuse the default server by ambient socket name, under hostile ambient on all five members | `ResolveSocket` (socket.go) | TestResolveSocketDerivesIgnoringAmbient |\n40|| 18 | Ambient facts observed without use | `ObserveAmbient` (socket.go) | TestObserveAmbientRecordsWithoutUsing, TestObserveAmbientNilLookupKeepsOutOfBand |\n41|| 19 | Environment-variable vector refuses on both callers with no spawn and no directory | `Acquire` via `ResolveSocket` | TestAcquireRefusesEveryAmbientOverrideVector/environment_variable (foreground, background) |\n42|| 20 | Inherited-socket vector refuses on both callers with no spawn and no directory | `Acquire` via `ResolveSocket` | TestAcquireRefusesEveryAmbientOverrideVector/inherited_socket (foreground, background) |\n43|| 21 | Default-path vector refuses on both callers with no spawn and no directory | `Acquire` via `ResolveSocket` | TestAcquireRefusesEveryAmbientOverrideVector/default_path (foreground, background) |\n44|| 22 | Conventional-name vector refuses on both callers with no spawn and no directory | `Acquire` via `ResolveSocket` | TestAcquireRefusesEveryAmbientOverrideVector/conventional_name (foreground, background) |\n45|| 55 | TMUX_TMPDIR vector refuses on both callers with no spawn and no directory | `Acquire` via `ResolveSocket` | TestAcquireRefusesEveryAmbientOverrideVector/tmux_tmpdir (foreground, background) |\n46|| 58 | Whitespace-only override refuses on both callers with no spawn and no directory | `Acquire` via `ResolveSocket` | TestAcquireRefusesEveryAmbientOverrideVector/whitespace_only (foreground, background), TestResolveSocketRefusesEveryOverrideVector/whitespace_only |\n47|| 23 | Ambient value colliding with the derived socket refuses on every member, byte-identical and unclean (`/./`, `//`) spellings alike, and the TMUX member in the real `<socket>,<pid>,<index>` encoding, on both callers. Only TMUXEnv and InheritedSocket can name the derived socket in real tmux semantics; the other three members pin defence-in-depth shapes. Roots containing a comma are outside the TMUX member's encoding (bound B16) | `Acquire` via `ResolveSocket` | TestAcquireRefusesAmbientCollision (5 members × foreground/background), TestResolveSocketRefusesAmbientCollision (5 subtests), TestResolveSocketRefusesAmbientCollisionUncleanSpellings (2 subtests), TestAcquireRefusesAmbientCollisionUncleanSpelling (foreground, background), TestResolveSocketRefusesTMUXEnvRealEncoding, TestAcquireRefusesTMUXEnvCollisionRealEncoding (foreground, background) |\n48|| 40 | Absent server spawns dedicated with exact -S argv disjoint from every ambient vector, pinned element-by-element through the entry | `Acquire` via `BuildArgv` | TestAcquireForegroundSpawnsDedicatedServer |\n49|| 41 | Running attested dedicated server attaches with no second spawn | `Acquire` | TestAcquireForegroundAttachesToRunningAttested |\n50|| 46 | Spawn vector carries the dedicated -S socket | `BuildArgv` (argv.go) | TestBuildArgvAddressesOnlyTheDerivedSocket |\n51|| 47 | Ambient sockets refuse at the spawn vector on all five members | `BuildArgv` (argv.go) | TestBuildArgvRefusesAmbientSocket (5 subtests) |\n52|\n53|## §4.2 credential-sensitive creation; background broker-or-refuse\n54|\n55|| # | Clause (spec words) | Call site | Test |\n56||---|---------------------|-----------|------|\n57|| 24 | A background CLI MAY contact an already-running authenticated Aqua broker and its attested AX tmux server (macOS) | `Acquire` via `CheckBrokerContact` | TestAcquireBackgroundContactsBroker |\n58|| 25 | If neither exists it MUST return `capability_unavailable` with typed realm/readiness details: no broker | `Acquire` | TestAcquireBackgroundMissReturnsTypedUnavailable/no_broker |\n59|| 26 | Same: foreign-user broker | `Acquire` | TestAcquireBackgroundMissReturnsTypedUnavailable/foreign-user_broker |\n60|| 27 | Same: unattested server, including the zero-admission and decoy-only members | `Acquire` | TestAcquireBackgroundMissReturnsTypedUnavailable/unattested_server, .../zero_server_admission, .../decoy-only_server_admission |\n61|| 28 | Same: stale-generation admission, including the admitted-without-generation member | `Ac