suite 0 skip. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree.\\n17:### TASK-260830-35urbp rev5 — Private tmux server management rework (custody oracle, Request.Name removal, platform-axis absence pin, spy census)\\n24:### TASK-260830-35urbp rev4 — Private tmux server management rework (spec socket path, background absence code, Running-arm entry pins, TMUX encoding, bounds)\\n30:### TASK-260830-35urbp rev3 — Private tmux server management rework (verify-side non-directory pin, both-empty arms, narrower-mode pin, cleaned collision)\\n36:### TASK-260830-35urbp rev2 — Private tmux server management rework (P1 attestation fork + Windows vet, 9 surviving narrowings)\\n43:### TASK-260830-35urbp rev1 (SUPERSEDED by the rev2 entry above — describes the rejected rev1 tree, never landed)\\n649:- F3/INSTRUMENT: `hosttrust.HeldExclusive` capability (only `exclusiveHold` forges; verified live pre-write; expired on unlock) threaded through all pair writers; `store.lock.exclusive()` signature kept for read paths and probe compat. Static gate rewritten fail-closed (all decls incl. package-var initializers, transitive alias resolution, helper-escape detection, exact (receiver,method) backend pairs, direct-os-mutation rule, hold-entry closures for JointCommit+WithExclusiveHold) with 6 executable rogue controls (4 reviewer verbatim + direct-os.WriteFile + backend-receiver rogue); rev6 token-less plants no longer compile (vet error captured as evidence).\\n653:### TASK-260909-2ez769 rework rev6 — CR5 unlocked-compensation finding repaired as a class\\n655:- CENSUS: 12-row write-path census (`TASK-260909-2ez769_write-path-census-rev6.md` board outcome) covers every pair mutation incl. legacy `migrate` (fail-closed row, pinned by `TestLegacyMigrateBesideMarkerRefusesConvergence`), inert credential staging, atomic lock creation, and the sabotage remainder (vanished-marker re-stage). Enforced by committed static gate `TestWritePathCensusGate` + control `TestWritePathGateFlagsUnlockedCaller`; preserve-token order-swap plant `compensate-verify-before-restore` passes the gate and fails only behaviorally.\\n====\\nfunc TestAcquireBackgroundInvalidGenerationRefusesAfterProbe(t *testing.T) {\\n\\troot := runtimeRoot(t)\\n\\truntimeDir(t, root)\\n\\treq := validRequest(t, root)\\n\\treq.Caller = CallerBackground\\n\\treq.Generation = \\\"gen\\\\xff\\\"\\n\\tspy := &spawnSpy{}\\n\\tprobe := &probeServerSpy{}\\n\\tprobed := false\\n\\treq.Deps.Spawn = spy.spawn\\n\\treq.Deps.ProbeServer = probe.probe\\n\\treq.Deps.ProbeBroker = func() (BrokerReport, error) {\\n\\t\\tprobed = true\\n\\t\\treturn BrokerReport{}, nil\\n\\t}\\n\\t_, err := Acquire(req)\\n\\trequireLocalError(t, err, \\\"tmux_invalid_arguments\\\", \\\"realm details\\\")\\n\\tif !probed {\\n\\t\\tt.Fatal(\\\"broker was not probed before the detail refusal\\\")\\n\\t}\\n\\tif spy.calls != 0 {\\n\\t\\tt.Fatalf(\\\"spawn calls = %d, want 0\\\", spy.calls)\\n\\t}\\n\\tprobe.requireSilent(t)\\n}\\n\\nfunc TestAcquireBackgroundProbeFailurePassesThrough(t *testing.T) {\\n\\troot := runtimeRoot(t)\\n\\truntimeDir(t, root)\\n\\treq := validRequest(t, root)\\n\\treq.Caller = CallerBackground\\n\\tspy := &spawnSpy{}\\n\\tprobe := &probeServerSpy{}\\n\\treq.Deps.Spawn = spy.spawn\\n\\treq.Deps.ProbeServer = probe.probe\\n\\treq.Deps.ProbeBroker = func() (BrokerReport, error) {\\n\\t\\treturn BrokerReport{}, errProbeBoom\\n\\t}\\n\\t_, err := Acquire(req)\\n\\tif !errors.Is(err, errProbeBoom) {\\n\\t\\tt.Fatalf(\\\"err = %v, want the probe failure, not unavailable\\\", err)\\n\\t}\\n\\tif spy.calls != 0 {\\n\\t\\tt.Fatalf(\\\"spawn calls = %d, want 0\\\", spy.calls)\\n\\t}\\n\\tprobe.requireSilent(t)\\n}\\n\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 4318,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1080,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
