{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cb93","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c5d0-c246-7b92-beac-dc3b11390997"},"sequence":1060,"recorded_at":1780531400002115,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"aa3bb7a1-c12a-4660-a0d5-ffba7d41ef0c","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"aa3bb7a1-c12a-4660-a0d5-ffba7d41ef0c","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"aa3bb7a1-c12a-4660-a0d5-ffba7d41ef0c"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c5d6-5dbf-7a72-991c-82de93dc9129"},"task_id":"01a0c5d6-5dbf-7a72-991c-82de93dc9129","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c5d6-5dbf-7a72-991c-82de93dc9129","chunk":"Read text file `LOGBOOK.md`.\n1|# Flight Logbook\n2|\n3|> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\n4|> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\n5|\n6|## 2026-09-21\n7|\n8|### TASK-260830-35urbp rev6 — Gate × entry census instrument + broker-wiring, ownership, and session-entry pins\n9|\n10|- REWORKED after review-verdict-rev5 (CHANGES REQUESTED: no P1, one P2 class with four measured members, two P3; trunk unmoved at `799c338`, no refresh; every rev4 finding stays closed with its driven evidence kept — production behaved correctly at every point the review drove). The deliverable this round is the instrument: a gate × entry census (24 gates × 11 entries = 264 cells: 50 measured with a named test plus an admitting narrowing row each, 4 stated bounds, 210 unreachable with structural reasons) in TRACEABILITY.md, mirrored in the conformance matrix. Building it surfaced and closed member gaps beyond the four the reviewer measured.\n11|- P2-A (broker-or-refuse pinned at the entry only for fixture shapes): three server-admission subtests (zero admission, admitted-without-generation, decoy-only) added to `TestAcquireBackgroundMissReturnsTypedUnavailable` AND mirrored in `TestCheckBrokerContactRefusesEachMissingFact`; shipped `N-broker-zero-admission` at the `CheckBrokerContact` server wiring (R09 shape; R10/R19 share the anchor — replay-verified killed by the new tests); a fail-if-called `ProbeServer` spy armed in every background-path `Acquire` test (23/23 mechanical census, incl. the miss tables and `TestAcquireBackgroundVerifiesWithoutCreating`); shipped `D-background-fallback-foreground` (R18 shape: fallback into `acquireForeground` guarded on `ProbeServer`) with the row-31/README sentence extended to both foreground dependencies.\n12|- P3-A (ownership member of the absence class): new `TestAcquireBackgroundStagesOwnershipRefusal` (unix-only file, `effectiveUID` seam) asserting the top-level `tmux_unsafe_runtime_dir at runtime ownership` with no broker contact and both spies silent, plus shipped `N-absence-remap-ownership` (R01 shape); the census added the sibling rows `N-absence-remap-containment` and `N-absence-remap-invalid` so every classifier member carries a row. P3-B (false \"before any side effect\"): session identity now parses at the foreground entry before `EnsureRuntimeDir` and the probe, with no-directory/no-probe assertions in `TestAcquireForegroundRefusesMalformedSession` and shipped `N-session-entry` (kills through the side-effect assertions while the refusal code stays correct).\n13|- Census-driven closures beyond the verdict: caller-dimension subtests on the pre-dispatch gates (override/collision/details/unknown-platform tables drive both callers); `N-dispatch-foreground`/`N-dispatch-background` for the caller→path routing; `N-wiring-lexical/ensure/verify` for the three `RuntimeDirName` sites; `N-details-generation/brokerstate/constructor` (incl. the input-reachable invalid-UTF-8 arm, pinned with a probe-order assertion); `N-root-symlink-commit/verify` plus verify- and background-entry symlink-root tests; `N-argv-detached/tail` with a full element-by-element vector assertion through the spawn entry; background-entry symlink-leaf and handle-mismatch tests; mask extensions so shared-site rows kill through every entry they cover (attribution verified per entry from the raw logs).\n14|- Observations: row 23/B16 scope comma roots out of the TMUX member's encoding and symlinked-or-relative aliases out of the cleaned-string gate; B9 states `Dependencies.Spawn` as inert on the background path; B15 names the commit-side leaf-`Stat` and `NewGuard` arms; static-gate exit codes recorded in the evidence archive.\n15|- Battery: 72 narrowing + 2 additive KILLED + control SURVIVED, 75/75 twice with identical verdicts and per-plant raw logs. AC: 58 of 58 rows driven through production entries by named tests (matrix rev6). Full 30-command suite green firsthand (race gate in 6 bounded groups with identical flags, 45/45, no DATA RACE); `GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go vet` exit 0; tmux-hidden suite 0 skip. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree.\n16|\n17|### TASK-260830-35urbp rev5 — Private tmux server management rework (custody oracle, Request.Name removal, platform-axis absence pin, spy census)\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cb95","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c5d0-c246-7b92-beac-dc3b11390997"},"sequence":1061,"recorded_at":1780531400002117,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"aa3bb7a1-c12a-4660-a0d5-ffba7d41ef0c","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"aa3bb7a1-c12a-4660-a0d5-ffba7d41ef0c","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"aa3bb7a1-c12a-4660-a0d5-ffba7d41ef0c"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c5d6-5dbf-7a72-991c-82de93dc9129"},"task_id":"01a0c5d6-5dbf-7a72-991c-82de93dc9129","event":{"kind":"completed","task_id":"01a0c5d6-5dbf-7a72-991c-82de93dc9129"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cb97","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c5d0-c246-7b92-beac-dc3b11390997"},"sequence":1062,"recorded_at":1780531400002119,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"aa3bb7a1-c12a-4660-a0d5-ffba7d41ef0c","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"aa3bb7a1-c12a-4660-a0d5-ffba7d41ef0c","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"aa3bb7a1-c12a-4660-a0d5-ffba7d41ef0c"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c5d6-5da3-7322-a79b-a4283fc81442"},"task_id":"01a0c5d6-5da3-7322-a79b-a4283fc81442","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c5d6-5da3-7322-a79b-a4283fc81442","chunk":"Read text file `README.md`.\n(2328 line(s) above)\n2329|## Private tmux server management (`tmuxserver` leaf)\n2330|\n2331|[`internal/tmuxserver`](internal/tmuxserver) creates owner-only runtime\n2332|directories and manages dedicated `tmux -S` servers with no ambient or\n2333|default-server discovery or reuse (pinned Sections 3.2, 4.2, 4.C-4.E).\n2334|The dedicated socket is `<runtime>/tmux/ax.sock` under the Runtime IPC\n2335|root (per-user temporary directory on macOS, `$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/ax` on\n2336|Linux/WSL2), resolved by the landed `localstore` layout and supplied by\n2337|the caller; the socket is runtime IPC, never durable identity.\n2338|`EnsureRuntimeDir` commits the runtime leaf relative to a pinned root\n2339|handle (`mkdirat`, never a path-string `MkdirAll`) and enforces three\n2340|independent custody gates — containment, exact `0700` mode, effective-UID\n2341|ownership — each of which refuses alone; an existing directory is\n2342|verified, never silently repaired. `ResolveSocket` derives the one\n2343|server socket from the runtime directory and refuses any explicit\n2344|override on all five ambient members (`TMUX` and `TMUX_TMPDIR`\n2345|environment values, inherited socket, default path, conventional\n2346|`default` name). `Acquire` reaches the server through the\n2347|caller-appropriate path: foreground ensures the directory, then attaches\n2348|to the running attested server or spawns the dedicated `-S` server whose\n2349|stable pane entrypoint is `ax pane SESSION_ID`, while background\n2350|verifies the existing directory without creating it, contacts only the\n2351|already-running authenticated same-user broker and its attested server,\n2352|and a miss — including an absent runtime directory, the ordinary\n2353|post-reboot cold state — returns the typed `capability_unavailable`\n2354|refusal with realm/readiness details, while an existing-but-unsafe\n2355|directory keeps its custody refusal — there is no fallback to direct\n2356|creation, and every background-path `Acquire` test (23/23 by\n2357|mechanical census) arms both a spy spawner and a spy server probe\n2358|that fail the run if either is ever invoked. Attestation is the landed `terminalbackend`\n2359|Reconcile/ResolveEvidence admission consumed as an `Admitted` set\n2360|composed only with generation equality: a missing realm row or a\n2361|stale-generation admission refuses, so a cached observation replayed as\n2362|live authorizes nothing. Every broker, server, and spawner interaction\n2363|runs through injected dependencies, so the suite passes with no tmux\n2364|process anywhere; native Windows refuses every request.\n2365|\n2366|Run the focused tests and coverage with:\n2367|\n2368|```bash\n2369|go test ./internal/tmuxserver -count=1\n2370|go test ./internal/tmuxserver -cover -count=1\n2371|```\n2372|\n2373|Run the narrowing battery (72 narrowing mutants, two supplementary\n2374|additive rows, plus one harmless control) with:\n2375|\n2376|```bash\n2377|PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 internal/tmuxserver/mutant_harness.py\n2378|```\n2379|\n2380|The harness mutates one production file in place, runs the named killer\n2381|through the production entry point, restores the file from backup, and\n2382|reports per-row verdicts with subprocess exits; `AX_MUTANT_VERBOSE=1`\n2383|additionally prints the raw per-plant logs, and `--log-dir` captures one\n2384|raw log per plant. Task validation logs and mutation artifacts are\n2385|attached to `TASK-260830-35urbp`. The package adds no `ax` command, no\n2386|`doctor` result, and no runtime capability claim; the clause-to-test\n2387|matrix with its stated bounds lives in\n2388|[the task evidence map](internal/tmuxserver/TRACEABILITY.md).\n2389|\n2390|## Ownership reducer properties\n2391|\n2392|The four story-pinned ownership invariants (pinned v0.6.0 Sections 2.2, 5.3,\n2393|and 13.6-13.10) hold as executable property tests over the landed production\n2394|reducers — `sessstate.Reduce` with `Compare` and the union projection,\n2395|`sessrepo.WinningLease` with `ListLeases`, and `fencing.Authorize*`:\n2396|\n2397|1. Union-order independence: every permutation of a union multiset, and every\n2398|   partition into successive unions, projects byte-identically (winner,\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
